WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.007
[theme song playing]

00:07.090 --> 00:11.011
[in English]
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:11.094 --> 00:14.681
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:15.474 --> 00:20.354
♪ Deep in the silence
But it doesn't mean you're lost ♪

00:20.437 --> 00:23.690
♪ And I'll tell you what ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:27.236
♪ We're on the train ♪

00:27.319 --> 00:31.073
♪ I promise I'll be where you are ♪

00:31.782 --> 00:35.869
♪ If any thought is against you ♪

00:35.953 --> 00:39.623
♪ With you, I am starting over ♪

00:39.706 --> 00:43.460
♪ We're learning to walk again ♪

00:43.544 --> 00:44.419
[song concludes]

00:44.503 --> 00:45.963
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:46.964 --> 00:49.174
[Chung-gu in Korean]
Are you sure about this?

00:50.759 --> 00:52.636
[tense music playing]

00:52.719 --> 00:54.471
Once you walk out that door…

00:54.972 --> 00:56.932
we won't be on the same team.

00:58.392 --> 01:00.227
You know I don't play fair, right?

01:00.310 --> 01:02.479
It won't be easy
getting into a decent firm.

01:02.563 --> 01:06.817
I don't speak kindly about someone
who turned their back on me.

01:07.734 --> 01:10.320
-I'll find somewhere to work.
-That's not the issue.

01:11.321 --> 01:13.699
You're not the kind of person
who'll take any job.

01:13.782 --> 01:16.118
What matters to you is where you go.

01:16.201 --> 01:18.370
From college to law firms,

01:18.453 --> 01:21.748
you think that your affiliations
define your worth, don't you?

01:21.832 --> 01:24.334
Only two of the top three
law firms are left.

01:24.418 --> 01:28.255
How far down
are you willing to go after that?

01:29.214 --> 01:31.383
If it's not up to your standards,

01:31.466 --> 01:33.594
I bet you'd rather
change careers entirely.

01:35.929 --> 01:38.056
I'm curious to see…

01:39.975 --> 01:41.226
how far…

01:42.728 --> 01:44.146
you are willing to fall.

01:46.732 --> 01:48.317
[Ho-su] I'll help you.

01:48.400 --> 01:49.318
[music concludes]

01:49.401 --> 01:52.404
That whistleblowing case
you never got to finish.

01:52.487 --> 01:54.197
I'll help you with it.

01:55.282 --> 01:57.868
Who asked for your help?

01:58.785 --> 02:00.704
I told you. That's all behind me.

02:00.787 --> 02:04.541
I was still with the firm then,
so I couldn't take the case myself.

02:04.625 --> 02:07.210
Now I can handle the lawsuit
or whatever else needs to be done.

02:07.294 --> 02:08.378
Look…

02:08.920 --> 02:10.213
I said I'm fine.

02:10.297 --> 02:14.217
And wait. You quit?
Why'd you suddenly leave?

02:14.301 --> 02:15.594
Why not?

02:15.677 --> 02:17.554
That's not the only law firm in the world.

02:17.638 --> 02:20.599
I can go anywhere.
No, somewhere even better.

02:21.308 --> 02:23.060
That's what I'll do.

02:23.644 --> 02:24.728
I will.

02:24.811 --> 02:26.063
[pensive music playing]

02:26.146 --> 02:28.357
Are… you drunk?

02:29.274 --> 02:30.651
No.

02:30.734 --> 02:35.238
I'm more clear-headed than ever,
and I don't regret my decision.

02:35.864 --> 02:38.408
-I'm going to help you.
-I said I don't need help.

02:38.492 --> 02:40.369
[Ho-su] I'm still going to help.

02:40.452 --> 02:41.870
I'll do whatever it takes.

02:41.953 --> 02:43.080
I have to.

02:43.955 --> 02:47.793
[Mi-ji] Every animal has
its own way of surviving.

02:47.876 --> 02:50.295
Mi-ji has missed
nearly two months of school.

02:50.962 --> 02:54.174
If she's sick,
she should submit a doctor's note.

02:54.257 --> 02:56.134
She's barely meeting
the attendance requirement.

02:56.218 --> 02:59.262
If this keeps up, she won't graduate.

03:00.305 --> 03:03.016
[music fades]

03:05.394 --> 03:06.478
[exhales]

03:06.561 --> 03:09.022
[soft daring music playing]

03:13.443 --> 03:15.612
-[teacher] Lee Da-yeon.
-[student] Here.

03:15.696 --> 03:17.906
-[teacher] Yu Mi-ji.
-Present.

03:23.078 --> 03:25.956
[Mi-ji] When they sense danger
or predators,

03:27.048 --> 03:30.008
chameleons change their appearance
to fool their enemies.

03:30.085 --> 03:31.336
CONSENT LIST

03:31.920 --> 03:33.130
[music concludes]

03:33.213 --> 03:37.175
Doesn't Mi-ji get
some kind of terminal leave?

03:37.259 --> 03:39.886
-Pardon?
-Unless she joined the army,

03:39.970 --> 03:41.346
how can she be gone this long?

03:41.430 --> 03:42.472
[chuckles]

03:43.140 --> 03:46.101
She went to Seoul. To a relative's house.

03:46.184 --> 03:51.690
What kind of relative lets someone stay
for over a year?

03:51.773 --> 03:54.359
-[chuckles nervously]
-[intriguing music playing]

03:54.443 --> 03:56.945
-[Ok-hui] There you go.
-Okay. Thanks.

03:57.028 --> 03:59.322
-Bye.
-[Ok-hui] All right. Take care.

03:59.406 --> 04:03.118
[Mi-ji] Some animals, like pheasants,
just tuck their heads to blend in.

04:03.201 --> 04:06.079
By the way, is Mi-ji still not back yet?

04:06.830 --> 04:10.375
It's been two years since she left!
Has she moved out for good?

04:10.459 --> 04:11.460
Moved out?

04:11.543 --> 04:14.671
Didn't she go to Seoul
to get her leg fixed?

04:14.755 --> 04:16.757
-What the heck!
-[Mi-ji] Octopuses and squids…

04:16.840 --> 04:20.051
-Are you out of your mind?
-…release ink to escape danger.

04:21.219 --> 04:23.722
[intriguing music continues]

04:27.601 --> 04:28.935
[Mi-ji] And humans,

04:30.687 --> 04:32.689
when in crisis,

04:32.773 --> 04:38.737
often behave in ways
no other animal does.

04:39.988 --> 04:43.992
[Ok-hui] Gosh, it's tough cooking
all three meals at home every day.

04:45.368 --> 04:48.789
No deliveries, no eating out…

04:49.498 --> 04:51.583
It's not good to eat out all the time.

04:51.666 --> 04:54.169
It's cheaper and healthier to eat at home.

04:54.252 --> 04:55.462
Did you get garlic?

04:56.087 --> 04:59.382
[Ok-hui] Wait. Did I buy garlic?

05:03.178 --> 05:04.471
EPISODE 4
MY NEMESIS

05:04.554 --> 05:05.430
[door lock rattles]

05:05.514 --> 05:06.973
[music concludes]

05:07.933 --> 05:10.101
[Mi-ji] New York? Or London?

05:10.227 --> 05:11.478
Man!

05:12.354 --> 05:13.438
New York?

05:14.231 --> 05:15.565
London?

05:15.649 --> 05:17.067
[sighs]

05:17.150 --> 05:19.069
Choosing between
the London and New York branch?

05:19.152 --> 05:20.278
-No.
-Don't get up.

05:20.362 --> 05:21.279
[quirky music playing]

05:21.363 --> 05:22.656
[Tae-gwan] You deserve it.

05:22.739 --> 05:25.450
You already set up a meeting
with the landowner of Rosa Restaurant.

05:25.534 --> 05:27.661
Yes, it's set for Friday afternoon.

05:28.161 --> 05:31.081
I had high hopes,
and you really delivered.

05:31.957 --> 05:35.585
Our Ms. Yu exceeded our expectations,
don't you think?

05:35.669 --> 05:36.837
Well…

05:37.337 --> 05:40.298
She hasn't agreed to sell yet.
All we have is a meeting scheduled.

05:40.382 --> 05:43.969
Securing a meeting with someone
who refused to speak to us is impressive.

05:44.052 --> 05:46.972
-[yelps softly]
-Hey, everyone!

05:47.055 --> 05:49.933
Let's give Ms. Yu a round of applause
for her hard work.

05:53.812 --> 05:55.355
It's fine. Stay seated.

06:01.111 --> 06:02.904
-[music concludes]
-Thank you.

06:03.488 --> 06:05.782
Don't worry too much, Mr. Choi.

06:05.866 --> 06:09.536
I will make sure our team
gets the credit, not her.

06:09.619 --> 06:11.162
No way. We need to go bigger.

06:11.246 --> 06:12.873
Invite the General Affairs Team.

06:13.415 --> 06:16.041
And keep emphasizing,
"Ms. Yu made this meeting happen."

06:16.541 --> 06:17.669
[intriguing music playing]

06:17.752 --> 06:20.213
-Sorry?
-Get her under the spotlight now.

06:20.297 --> 06:23.174
So when things go wrong,
all the attention's on her.

06:23.258 --> 06:24.718
You know how landowners are.

06:25.802 --> 06:29.014
They say they will turn up
and then ghost you at the last minute.

06:29.598 --> 06:32.642
Still, if by some miracle
Mi-rae pulls off the land acquisition--

06:32.726 --> 06:34.394
-Mr. Shin.
-[Gyeong-min] Yes.

06:35.520 --> 06:37.522
Who's leading the new HQ building project?

06:37.606 --> 06:39.274
Lead Specialist Park…

06:43.570 --> 06:45.822
So, even if Mi-rae pulls it off,

06:45.906 --> 06:47.699
she'll end up backing out.

06:48.867 --> 06:50.118
[Gyeong-min chuckles]

06:50.911 --> 06:53.413
Sir, you are ten steps ahead.

06:54.414 --> 06:56.082
I'm learning so much from you.

06:58.960 --> 07:00.462
[mouths] Lead Specialist Park?

07:04.966 --> 07:06.384
Ghost me?

07:07.135 --> 07:08.970
No way.

07:11.139 --> 07:12.182
[chuckles]

07:13.266 --> 07:14.517
No.

07:14.601 --> 07:15.560
[grumbles]

07:15.644 --> 07:17.854
[music turns suspenseful]

07:17.938 --> 07:20.065
Please, that can't be true.

07:20.148 --> 07:22.525
[pants]

07:22.609 --> 07:23.902
[grunts]

07:23.985 --> 07:25.320
Is she really ghosting me?

07:25.403 --> 07:27.906
Ma'am, please. That can't be true.

07:27.989 --> 07:29.032
[sighs]

07:29.616 --> 07:33.244
Please, ma'am. Don't do this to me.

07:33.328 --> 07:36.957
[muttering] Ms. Ro-sa.

07:37.040 --> 07:38.333
-[gasps]
-[music concludes]

07:38.416 --> 07:39.751
Ma'am.

07:39.834 --> 07:42.963
-[breathing heavily]
-[intriguing music playing]

07:49.135 --> 07:50.345
[music fades]

07:50.428 --> 07:54.766
Gosh, a leak out of nowhere?
This is terrible.

07:54.849 --> 07:56.142
[Ro-sa mutters]

07:57.477 --> 07:59.729
Are you here to keep me put
before the meeting?

07:59.813 --> 08:01.731
[innocently] What? No!

08:01.815 --> 08:04.067
I was just heading home and…

08:05.068 --> 08:07.195
How long should I say
you'll be closed for?

08:08.405 --> 08:09.990
Until the day after tomorrow…

08:10.073 --> 08:11.533
No.

08:11.616 --> 08:12.951
Make it three days.

08:13.034 --> 08:15.412
Gosh, three days?

08:15.495 --> 08:17.664
Does it really take that long
to fix a leak?

08:18.456 --> 08:20.792
I also need a new fridge.

08:21.960 --> 08:23.336
Jeez. [sighs]

08:23.420 --> 08:26.715
The old one was ancient,
so they don't make parts for it anymore.

08:26.798 --> 08:29.801
It short-circuited and burned. [sighs]

08:29.884 --> 08:32.929
Where will you go to buy one?
I can come with you.

08:33.013 --> 08:35.598
Doesn't your company give you any work?

08:35.682 --> 08:37.976
[timidly] I am working right now.

08:38.059 --> 08:39.394
TEMPORARILY CLOSED

08:40.186 --> 08:42.689
If you're done
checking up on me, take this.

08:42.772 --> 08:45.066
-Just put it in a pot and let it boil.
-Yes!

08:46.317 --> 08:48.278
I finally get a single portion takeout?

08:48.361 --> 08:49.696
Thank you.

08:51.072 --> 08:52.615
No need to pay.

08:52.699 --> 08:55.577
I'm giving it to you
so it doesn't go to waste.

08:55.660 --> 08:58.121
And give this to that guy.

08:58.204 --> 09:00.248
Ho-su, Ho-se, or whatever it was.

09:00.331 --> 09:02.500
[chuckles] You mean Lee Ho-su?

09:05.670 --> 09:07.213
-Ah!
-[quirky music playing]

09:07.297 --> 09:09.090
He's getting ginseng chicken soup?

09:10.592 --> 09:13.136
He must be feeling anxious
because he quit his job.

09:13.219 --> 09:15.472
He should at least eat well.

09:15.555 --> 09:17.223
Drop it off and check in on him.

09:17.849 --> 09:19.476
Don't worry.

09:19.559 --> 09:23.188
He probably even makes
a to-do list on his days off.

09:23.897 --> 09:26.232
People like him can end up

09:26.316 --> 09:28.943
like deflated balloons
when faced with such hardship.

09:30.070 --> 09:31.446
Really? Ho-su?

09:31.529 --> 09:33.073
[door lock chimes]

09:33.156 --> 09:34.908
[music concludes]

09:37.911 --> 09:39.829
-Come in.
-Okay.

09:41.414 --> 09:44.042
-Want something to drink?
-Just water.

09:52.050 --> 09:53.134
[clears throat]

09:57.263 --> 09:58.598
What's that?

09:58.681 --> 10:00.391
It's ginseng chicken soup.

10:00.475 --> 10:02.519
Ms. Ro-sa told me to bring it to you.

10:02.602 --> 10:04.771
You haven't eaten, right? Have some.

10:05.355 --> 10:07.982
-It's fine. I'll eat later.
-Have some now.

10:08.066 --> 10:10.485
It won't taste good
once it's been in the fridge.

10:10.568 --> 10:12.529
-I'll eat it later. I promise.
-Oh no!

10:13.154 --> 10:14.072
Gosh.

10:14.697 --> 10:17.659
-Sorry, let me get that.
-No, you get out of the way.

10:17.742 --> 10:18.827
I'll clean it up.

10:19.619 --> 10:20.787
[pieces clinking]

10:20.870 --> 10:22.038
[groans]

10:22.122 --> 10:24.457
You grabbed that with your bare hands?

10:24.541 --> 10:27.168
-[Ho-su sighs]
-Sit over there. I'll take care of it.

10:33.091 --> 10:36.886
Last time I saw you,
you were all fired up about helping me.

10:37.554 --> 10:39.389
Why do you seem so down now?

10:39.472 --> 10:40.598
Are you sick?

10:41.641 --> 10:43.893
I'm just tired from switching jobs.

10:45.228 --> 10:46.604
Switching jobs?

10:46.688 --> 10:48.523
You just quit a few days ago.

10:48.606 --> 10:50.150
When do you start at the new place?

10:52.360 --> 10:54.821
I've been rejected
everywhere I've applied so far.

10:55.822 --> 10:58.116
They must have needed
to fill those positions right away.

10:58.199 --> 11:01.911
But hey, it's good! You've never
really taken a break before, right?

11:01.995 --> 11:03.079
Now you can!

11:03.163 --> 11:05.290
Go travel or enjoy your hobbies.

11:06.249 --> 11:07.584
I don't have a hobby.

11:07.667 --> 11:11.087
It doesn't have to be anything big.
Just something you usually enjoy.

11:11.588 --> 11:13.882
What do you do when you're not working?

11:13.965 --> 11:15.341
I sleep…

11:16.301 --> 11:17.260
or do chores.

11:17.343 --> 11:19.596
No, not those.

11:19.679 --> 11:21.014
What do you do for fun?

11:21.097 --> 11:24.475
Like TV or games.
There has to be something you enjoy.

11:25.059 --> 11:25.977
Not really.

11:26.895 --> 11:30.190
What were you doing before I came over?

11:31.065 --> 11:32.859
-Thinking.
-About what?

11:33.526 --> 11:34.652
Everything.

11:35.904 --> 11:38.114
Things I've been too busy to think about.

11:38.990 --> 11:41.201
Things I didn't want to think about.

11:41.284 --> 11:42.327
[exhales]

11:42.410 --> 11:44.579
[gentle pop song playing]

11:45.246 --> 11:47.207
That won't do. Let's go.

11:47.290 --> 11:50.210
[in English]
♪ We used to travel city-wide ♪

11:50.293 --> 11:53.588
♪ A heartbeat on the street… ♪

11:53.671 --> 11:55.215
[in Korean] Here it is.

11:55.298 --> 11:57.342
-Hello.
-[vendor] Welcome.

11:58.092 --> 12:01.763
-Oh. How much is this?
-Gosh, you picked a fancy yarn.

12:01.846 --> 12:04.307
It's 30,000 won. What are you making?

12:04.390 --> 12:07.310
-[Mi-ji] Wrap it once, then pull through.
-[Ho-su] Okay.

12:07.393 --> 12:09.187
-Through here?
-[Mi-ji] Yes.

12:09.938 --> 12:12.357
-[Mi-ji] Let me.
-Wait. Didn't I hook one?

12:12.440 --> 12:14.567
-[song continues]
-I told you to hook two.

12:14.651 --> 12:16.945
[Mi-ji] Wrap it once.
Then pull it through.

12:17.028 --> 12:18.154
Ta-da!

12:18.238 --> 12:19.656
-[Ho-su] I see.
-Now it's a circle.

12:19.739 --> 12:22.867
If you keep doing this,
you'll end up with a scrubber.

12:23.368 --> 12:25.662
So, what's on your mind right now?

12:26.746 --> 12:27.872
Nothing, really.

12:28.456 --> 12:31.584
That's the power of crochet.

12:32.126 --> 12:33.670
It gives your mind a break.

12:35.505 --> 12:37.298
[song fades]

12:37.382 --> 12:38.591
[Mi-ji exhales]

12:39.092 --> 12:44.180
They say your brain waves while crocheting
are similar to those when you meditate.

12:44.264 --> 12:48.309
It's basically meditation with your hands.

12:49.102 --> 12:50.770
There. Go on.

12:54.148 --> 12:57.860
Being unemployed is a fight
against your own mind and the clock.

12:57.944 --> 13:00.488
When everyone else is working
and you're home alone,

13:00.571 --> 13:01.739
you think too much.

13:01.823 --> 13:04.659
And the more you think,
the more you lose track of time.

13:05.535 --> 13:07.912
You wonder if the clock's broken,

13:07.996 --> 13:10.748
but before you know it,
the whole day's gone.

13:10.832 --> 13:11.749
That's true.

13:11.833 --> 13:16.629
And 99% of those thoughts are useless.

13:17.755 --> 13:20.675
Thinking about the past
only brings regret,

13:20.758 --> 13:23.886
and thinking about the future
only brings anxiety.

13:23.970 --> 13:27.223
So whenever you start overthinking,

13:27.307 --> 13:28.933
just crochet.

13:29.017 --> 13:32.603
Just get through the day,
one stitch at a time.

13:32.687 --> 13:36.065
If you just hang in there,
something new will come along.

13:36.149 --> 13:37.525
And even if it doesn't,

13:37.608 --> 13:39.986
at least you'll have yourself a scrubber.

13:40.570 --> 13:41.988
How would you know?

13:42.488 --> 13:44.157
You've never been unemployed.

13:47.160 --> 13:48.161
Hey!

13:48.828 --> 13:51.080
I spent years on the civil service exam.

13:51.164 --> 13:53.499
And you can't call yourself…

13:54.584 --> 13:55.585
unemployed.

13:55.668 --> 13:58.046
You're just a lawyer who's between jobs.

13:58.629 --> 14:02.008
If you find a firm, that's great.
If not, just open an office.

14:02.091 --> 14:03.593
There's no need to be down.

14:05.928 --> 14:08.097
What if I end up being useless?

14:09.724 --> 14:11.476
[gentle music playing]

14:11.559 --> 14:13.895
I wanted to join a better firm

14:14.979 --> 14:17.440
and prove that I made the right choice.

14:19.359 --> 14:20.860
But now that I'm out,

14:22.236 --> 14:24.572
I think the firm I quit

14:25.239 --> 14:27.367
was the best I could ever achieve.

14:28.284 --> 14:31.621
It feels like
there's nowhere to go but down.

14:32.288 --> 14:34.332
So I'm scared to take the next step.

14:37.668 --> 14:38.836
[exhales heavily]

14:41.214 --> 14:42.465
Ho-su.

14:45.301 --> 14:46.761
You're still you.

14:48.346 --> 14:50.014
You're not any worse,

14:51.099 --> 14:53.101
you haven't disappeared,

14:53.184 --> 14:54.811
and you haven't gone downhill.

14:56.020 --> 14:57.897
You just quit a job.

14:59.190 --> 15:00.400
You're okay.

15:07.698 --> 15:08.866
Why…

15:09.659 --> 15:11.577
are you being so nice to me?

15:11.661 --> 15:12.703
What?

15:14.580 --> 15:18.334
Mi-rae, you're the last person
to try and comfort others.

15:21.462 --> 15:24.924
So what? You don't like it?

15:25.466 --> 15:27.635
-No, it's just…
-[music fades]

15:28.761 --> 15:32.348
-You seem different from usual.
-There you go again.

15:32.432 --> 15:35.143
You think you know me so well?

15:35.226 --> 15:37.145
What have you thought of me all this time?

15:37.228 --> 15:38.646
[exhales] Gosh.

15:39.188 --> 15:41.482
[tender music playing]

15:41.566 --> 15:42.942
[Ho-su] Oh.

15:43.025 --> 15:45.111
-You dropped a stitch.
-[Ho-su] What do I do?

15:45.194 --> 15:48.281
-Undo the whole thing?
-No, there's no need.

15:48.364 --> 15:50.741
Just go back to where you got lost.

15:51.534 --> 15:53.035
Give it to me.

15:53.119 --> 15:55.371
[Mi-ji sighs] I let my guard down.

15:55.455 --> 15:57.915
Why do I end up being myself around him?

15:57.999 --> 15:58.916
[grunts]

15:59.709 --> 16:00.960
Pay attention.

16:05.131 --> 16:06.257
Hook it in.

16:10.178 --> 16:13.097
[lively quirky music playing]

16:15.641 --> 16:17.935
[slide whistle blowing]

16:21.063 --> 16:22.482
-Not bad.
-Are you buying that?

16:22.565 --> 16:24.484
-[screams]
-[music concludes]

16:24.567 --> 16:26.068
You startled me.

16:26.152 --> 16:30.448
Didn't you say you'd rather
throw out your back than look silly?

16:30.531 --> 16:32.283
It's for my partner, not for me.

16:32.366 --> 16:33.784
[Myeong-gap] Buy two.

16:33.868 --> 16:37.038
They seem better than farming seat pads.

16:38.956 --> 16:40.208
[clears throat]

16:41.417 --> 16:44.128
Se-jin, are you getting those?

16:44.212 --> 16:48.424
Didn't you say you'd rather
throw out your back than look silly?

16:48.508 --> 16:51.719
Cut it out. Don't tease him.

16:51.802 --> 16:54.096
It's not for him. It's for Yu Candy.

16:54.180 --> 16:59.852
I see. Still, I'd never heard
that Mi-ji had two butts until today.

16:59.936 --> 17:02.271
People have two butt cheeks,
with one on each…

17:02.355 --> 17:03.606
-Forget it.
-[toys clatter]

17:03.689 --> 17:06.526
[laughs] Come on. Just get them.

17:06.609 --> 17:09.195
You've got the money.
Buy three or four for her.

17:09.737 --> 17:11.822
And you know what?

17:11.906 --> 17:15.785
Since working with you, Mi-ji's been
closed off and looking down again.

17:16.285 --> 17:18.704
I hope she doesn't disappear
like she did before.

17:18.788 --> 17:20.706
Gosh. Take that back, now!

17:21.707 --> 17:22.750
I take that back.

17:22.833 --> 17:25.336
Why do you keep saying
she'll disappear or run away?

17:25.419 --> 17:27.046
What did I do to her?

17:27.129 --> 17:31.217
Il-lam isn't saying
that you did something.

17:31.300 --> 17:35.846
He's just concerned
since Mi-ji has disappeared before.

17:36.514 --> 17:39.225
What do you mean, disappeared?
Did she go missing?

17:39.308 --> 17:42.311
Who knows whether she was missing
or if she ran away.

17:42.395 --> 17:45.856
She was gone for two or three years
and then came back.

17:45.940 --> 17:49.527
And her whole family clammed up

17:49.610 --> 17:52.280
and never explained what happened.

17:52.822 --> 17:56.617
They say she was in Seoul.

17:56.701 --> 18:00.329
But it was her twin who went to Seoul.

18:01.455 --> 18:02.915
She has a twin?

18:02.999 --> 18:06.794
I guess she just keeps quiet
and picks strawberries all day.

18:08.212 --> 18:09.714
Hurry up and check out.

18:09.797 --> 18:12.300
[quirky music playing]

18:13.259 --> 18:14.427
Never.

18:14.510 --> 18:15.636
[Myeong-gap] What?

18:15.720 --> 18:17.638
-Jeez.
-Come on.

18:23.102 --> 18:24.562
[music concludes]

18:24.645 --> 18:26.939
Well, it's comfortable.

18:27.023 --> 18:28.149
Right?

18:28.691 --> 18:32.320
I could tell just by looking at it.

18:32.403 --> 18:33.904
Why did you just get one for me?

18:34.322 --> 18:35.406
Ah.

18:35.489 --> 18:38.075
I just prefer picking the classic way.

18:38.159 --> 18:40.036
I'm a bit old-school, you know.

18:40.119 --> 18:42.496
[gentle quirky music playing]

18:48.419 --> 18:50.087
-Seoul?
-Yes.

18:50.171 --> 18:52.673
They say you have a twin in Seoul.

18:54.008 --> 18:56.218
Are you identical or fraternal?

18:57.637 --> 18:58.929
Identical.

18:59.430 --> 19:02.266
So you look exactly the same?
That's wild.

19:03.309 --> 19:04.685
What does your twin do?

19:05.269 --> 19:07.521
Do you have any siblings?

19:07.605 --> 19:08.689
Me?

19:09.607 --> 19:11.067
No, I'm an only child.

19:11.776 --> 19:13.027
Where in Seoul is your twin--

19:13.110 --> 19:15.196
Have you ever lived in Seoul?

19:15.738 --> 19:16.781
Me?

19:17.865 --> 19:20.743
I moved to Seoul after college.

19:21.494 --> 19:24.830
Well, technically I didn't graduate
because I started working.

19:25.414 --> 19:28.250
I used work as an excuse
because I didn't want to write my thesis…

19:28.334 --> 19:30.795
-Wait, what? I got sidetracked.
-[music concludes]

19:31.545 --> 19:33.506
Min-hee, you lived
in Seoul for a bit, right?

19:34.465 --> 19:36.300
-Me?
-Yes. Didn't you?

19:37.343 --> 19:40.554
Some say you were in Seoul,
and others say you were hospitalized.

19:40.638 --> 19:43.057
They said you were gone
for two or three years.

19:43.933 --> 19:45.851
Military service
isn't even that long these days.

19:45.935 --> 19:48.104
-What were you doing in Seoul--
-By the way,

19:48.187 --> 19:50.439
how far are you picking today?

19:50.981 --> 19:52.441
-Me?
-Yes.

19:54.735 --> 19:57.655
I don't want to overdo it,
so up to this row.

19:57.738 --> 20:00.366
Okay. I'll do that side, then.

20:03.494 --> 20:04.662
[Se-jin mutters, sighs]

20:08.124 --> 20:10.584
[Secretary Hwang]
Where have you been interviewing?

20:11.127 --> 20:14.213
Never mind.
You probably got rejected everywhere.

20:14.296 --> 20:16.841
Why did you quit so suddenly?

20:16.924 --> 20:19.176
You could've just transferred
to another team.

20:20.094 --> 20:21.095
Is it true?

20:21.846 --> 20:25.099
The rumor about your fistfight
with Attorney Lee Chung-gu?

20:25.182 --> 20:29.186
Is that why you wanted to meet me,
to ask if we really had a fistfight?

20:29.270 --> 20:31.147
That's part of it, I guess.

20:31.647 --> 20:33.858
Anyway, listen.

20:34.358 --> 20:37.027
You're not failing these interviews
because of your abilities,

20:37.111 --> 20:38.779
so don't rush things.

20:38.863 --> 20:41.532
Just wait until things blow over.

20:44.285 --> 20:47.913
By the way, what are you doing?

20:48.706 --> 20:52.752
I crochet whenever I have
a lot on my mind.

20:52.835 --> 20:54.795
Do you want a scrubber?

20:56.714 --> 20:57.715
[Secretary Hwang] Oh my.

20:57.798 --> 21:00.134
You must have had a lot on your mind.

21:01.343 --> 21:02.428
[chuckles]

21:02.511 --> 21:05.097
Who taught you how to crochet?

21:05.181 --> 21:06.098
Just a friend.

21:08.809 --> 21:10.144
[quirky music playing]

21:10.227 --> 21:13.272
Why are you making that face again?

21:13.355 --> 21:14.523
Is the friend a girl?

21:14.607 --> 21:15.900
Or a guy?

21:15.983 --> 21:19.403
Or a girl who's basically a guy?

21:19.487 --> 21:21.197
She's an old classmate.

21:21.697 --> 21:23.866
-Nothing's going on between us.
-Okay.

21:23.949 --> 21:25.826
There's nothing between you two,

21:25.910 --> 21:27.703
but you keep thinking about her
before bed.

21:27.787 --> 21:30.790
When you see her,
your feelings are all over the place,

21:30.873 --> 21:33.292
and you end up doing whatever she wants.

21:33.918 --> 21:36.837
Maybe she's changed,
or something's off with you.

21:36.921 --> 21:39.173
Do you know what you call

21:40.174 --> 21:41.884
this neuropsychiatric symptom?

21:42.384 --> 21:43.344
What is it?

21:44.220 --> 21:45.387
Having a thing.

21:46.347 --> 21:47.598
[both chuckle]

21:47.681 --> 21:48.766
You should go now.

21:48.849 --> 21:50.643
I'm glad to see you doing well.

21:51.185 --> 21:53.395
I'll head off with some scrubbers.

21:53.479 --> 21:54.647
One's for me.

21:56.148 --> 21:57.775
This one's cute.

21:57.858 --> 22:00.986
And one is for Ms. Min Ye-rin,
since her crush sailed away.

22:01.070 --> 22:02.238
Take care.

22:02.905 --> 22:03.906
I'm off.

22:09.745 --> 22:10.955
[door opens]

22:12.289 --> 22:14.208
-[music concludes]
-[cell phone buzzes]

22:15.125 --> 22:17.002
[Mi-ji] You said you were
up for anything, right?

22:17.086 --> 22:19.213
Come to Sindang Station, Exit 1,
in an hour.

22:19.296 --> 22:23.425
KITCHEN AND FURNITURE STREET

22:32.560 --> 22:33.561
[groans]

22:44.780 --> 22:46.156
Ho-su?

22:47.032 --> 22:48.534
Ms. Ro-sa.

22:48.617 --> 22:50.911
What brings you here at this time of day?

22:51.328 --> 22:52.580
[gentle music playing]

22:52.663 --> 22:56.208
[automated voice] The person
you are trying to reach is not available.

22:56.292 --> 22:57.501
She's not answering.

22:59.753 --> 23:01.130
She's unbelievable.

23:01.672 --> 23:03.841
Making a busy guy
come all the way out here…

23:05.593 --> 23:08.470
If you're talking about me, I'm not busy.

23:09.555 --> 23:12.057
-I'm unemployed now.
-Still.

23:12.141 --> 23:15.019
A lawyer shouldn't be dragged
into petty errands like this.

23:15.102 --> 23:16.478
It's fine, really.

23:17.104 --> 23:19.732
-I don't have much to do anyway.
-Just go home.

23:19.815 --> 23:21.567
You're just wasting time by coming here.

23:21.650 --> 23:23.903
-Go on, now.
-The thing is…

23:23.986 --> 23:26.280
I have too much time these days.

23:26.864 --> 23:29.658
As much as I enjoy crocheting at home,

23:29.742 --> 23:31.994
helping you is so much better.

23:35.289 --> 23:38.167
-[classmate 1] It's been forever.
-[classmate 2] Look at you all dolled up!

23:38.250 --> 23:40.002
The Sinsong Girls' High Queen
hasn't changed.

23:40.085 --> 23:41.670
18TH GRADUATING CLASS REUNION

23:41.754 --> 23:43.589
What do you mean, "dolled up"?

23:43.672 --> 23:45.633
I just threw on whatever I could grab.

23:45.716 --> 23:48.427
Gosh, you're still the queen of Sinsong.

23:48.510 --> 23:49.762
Queen Ok-hui, okay?

23:49.845 --> 23:51.555
-[both laugh]
-Stop it. [chuckles]

23:51.639 --> 23:53.974
How'd you manage to come on a weekday?

23:54.642 --> 23:56.602
Did the vice principal
give you permission?

23:56.685 --> 23:59.396
-[indistinct chatter]
-[intriguing quirky music playing]

23:59.480 --> 24:01.148
What permission?

24:01.231 --> 24:03.025
There's no school. It's Foundation Day.

24:03.108 --> 24:04.944
-Okay.
-I see.

24:05.027 --> 24:05.986
[laughs]

24:06.487 --> 24:08.989
[classmate 1]
Bun-hong hasn't changed a bit.

24:09.073 --> 24:11.075
People would think
that you're the vice principal

24:11.158 --> 24:13.369
and she's the lunch lady.

24:13.452 --> 24:15.037
[both laugh]

24:15.120 --> 24:17.706
What's a lunch lady supposed to look like?

24:18.624 --> 24:20.668
-Oh…
-Come on.

24:20.751 --> 24:24.380
Then I'll ask Ho-su to look into that too.

24:24.463 --> 24:25.339
[classmates exclaim]

24:25.422 --> 24:29.343
There must be a lawyer
specializing in insurance at the firm.

24:29.426 --> 24:32.846
So did Bun-hong come here for the reunion
or to give legal advice?

24:32.930 --> 24:34.014
[indistinct chatter]

24:34.098 --> 24:36.517
She finds all sorts of ways
to brag about her kid.

24:36.600 --> 24:37.726
[group laughs]

24:39.144 --> 24:40.312
Ok-hui!

24:40.813 --> 24:42.523
Did you come because it's Foundation Day?

24:42.606 --> 24:43.774
[laughs]

24:43.857 --> 24:48.696
Yes, I'm here, ma'am. [laughs awkwardly]

24:48.779 --> 24:50.072
What are you doing?

24:50.155 --> 24:52.491
The vice principal wants you
to assist her.

24:52.574 --> 24:54.076
-Hurry up.
-Go away.

24:54.159 --> 24:56.412
-[classmate 2] What is it? Why?
-Just go.

24:56.495 --> 24:57.997
-[laughs]
-What's with her today?

24:58.080 --> 24:59.957
-[indistinct chatter]
-[classmate yelps, laughs]

25:00.040 --> 25:02.459
-Move. I'm going to the restroom.
-[classmate 1] Don't push me.

25:02.543 --> 25:03.794
-[laughs]
-[music concludes]

25:03.877 --> 25:05.295
[Ok-hui] Let's have fun today.

25:05.379 --> 25:06.880
-[lively chatter]
-[Ok-hui laughs]

25:06.964 --> 25:08.215
[classmate] I'm counting on you.

25:08.298 --> 25:10.426
You two sat together? What about me?

25:11.218 --> 25:13.095
-How have you been?
-Mi-kyung!

25:13.178 --> 25:15.305
-So nice to see you.
-My goodness.

25:15.389 --> 25:17.558
-You've been well, right?
-Of course.

25:17.641 --> 25:19.560
[overlapping chatter]

25:19.643 --> 25:22.730
[classmate]
♪ Jjan, jjan, I won't cry anymore ♪

25:22.813 --> 25:25.274
[all] ♪ Goodbye, farewell, my love ♪

25:25.357 --> 25:26.608
♪ Jjan, jjan! ♪

25:26.692 --> 25:28.318
[group cheering]

25:28.402 --> 25:30.904
Now, next up…

25:31.530 --> 25:35.284
Let's find out just how loved
the Sinsong ladies really are.

25:35.868 --> 25:42.332
The first person to hear "I love you"
over the phone wins!

25:42.416 --> 25:45.377
-[group cheers]
-Excuse me. Attention please.

25:45.461 --> 25:48.922
Isn't this kind of unfair
for widows like us?

25:49.006 --> 25:51.258
-Not at all.
-Come on!

25:51.341 --> 25:53.302
It's totally unfair.

25:53.385 --> 25:56.638
What do you mean? I am a beloved woman.

25:56.722 --> 25:59.975
-[group gasps]
-It doesn't have to be your husband.

26:00.059 --> 26:01.602
That's right. Anyone's fine.

26:01.685 --> 26:04.438
It could be your kids
or the guy next door. Whoever!

26:04.521 --> 26:05.689
All right.

26:05.773 --> 26:09.234
As long as you hear “I love you,”
you're good.

26:09.318 --> 26:11.236
If you hear “I love you,” you win.

26:11.320 --> 26:14.490
I'll take ten seconds off
for the first challenger.

26:14.573 --> 26:17.076
-Who wants to go?
-Here, here!

26:17.159 --> 26:20.704
Let's hear Bun-hong
call her famous lawyer son!

26:20.788 --> 26:21.789
[women cheering]

26:21.872 --> 26:24.416
-No, what's with you?
-[tense quirky music playing]

26:24.500 --> 26:27.795
Come on. Didn't you say
you're a beloved woman?

26:27.878 --> 26:30.798
Or were you thinking
of someone other than your son?

26:30.881 --> 26:32.716
[laughs]

26:32.800 --> 26:34.426
[classmate] Whoever it is,

26:34.510 --> 26:37.096
let's have Vice Principal Yeom Bun-hong
give it a try!

26:37.179 --> 26:38.722
[women cheering]

26:38.806 --> 26:41.892
Beloved Yeom Bun-hong!

26:41.975 --> 26:43.519
Yeom Bun-hong!

26:43.602 --> 26:46.605
-[chuckles]
-Beloved Yeom Bun-hong!

26:46.688 --> 26:47.689
[music fades]

26:47.773 --> 26:49.983
[salesman] Ma'am, this one's the best.

26:50.067 --> 26:54.238
Strong compressor,
9-watt fan motor, indirect cooling,

26:54.321 --> 26:56.448
and all stainless steel. [laughs]

26:57.074 --> 26:58.867
Don't you have direct cooling models?

26:58.951 --> 27:01.328
These days, everyone uses fridges
with indirect cooling.

27:01.411 --> 27:03.038
They're frost-free, so it's convenient.

27:03.122 --> 27:04.581
But I heard at another store

27:04.665 --> 27:06.792
that for places that use up
ingredients daily,

27:06.875 --> 27:08.377
direct cooling is better.

27:09.128 --> 27:10.504
Price aside,

27:11.338 --> 27:13.799
don't frost-free refrigerators
use more electricity too?

27:13.882 --> 27:17.594
[laughing]
Ma'am, your son is very thorough.

27:17.678 --> 27:21.473
You must feel reassured
to have a son like him.

27:21.557 --> 27:25.269
I'll show you the direct cooling ones.
Right this way, ma'am.

27:25.352 --> 27:27.563
[laughs] Oh my.

27:28.188 --> 27:30.107
-This way, ma'am.
-[cell phone buzzing]

27:32.025 --> 27:33.402
MOM

27:36.989 --> 27:39.491
[dial tone ringing]

27:39.575 --> 27:40.659
[Ho-su] Hello?

27:41.743 --> 27:42.995
Ho-su, where are you?

27:43.579 --> 27:46.290
I hope I didn't call
while you were working.

27:46.373 --> 27:47.583
Oh…

27:48.083 --> 27:50.711
I'm actually with a client right now. Why?

27:53.505 --> 27:54.923
Oh…

27:55.007 --> 27:59.887
Ho-su, you know you're the only person
I love in this world, right?

28:01.722 --> 28:05.225
-What?
-I just feel like I never say it enough.

28:05.309 --> 28:08.937
Is there anything
you've wanted to say to me

28:09.021 --> 28:11.231
but haven't been able to?

28:12.649 --> 28:13.650
MY SON

28:13.734 --> 28:16.069
[Ho-su] What do you mean?

28:16.653 --> 28:19.364
[laughing] Hey.

28:19.448 --> 28:20.657
This could take a while.

28:20.741 --> 28:23.535
You know, things you've kept to yourself.

28:23.619 --> 28:26.663
Things you thought about saying
but couldn't.

28:26.747 --> 28:30.000
Something you've buried deep
in your heart.

28:30.083 --> 28:33.253
You know, like "I…"
[chuckles nervously]

28:33.962 --> 28:35.005
"I…"

28:39.301 --> 28:40.594
[Ho-su] Uh…

28:43.764 --> 28:45.515
I quit my job.

28:45.599 --> 28:46.475
[quirky music playing]

28:46.558 --> 28:47.643
What?

28:47.726 --> 28:50.479
[Ho-su] I left the law firm.

28:50.562 --> 28:51.605
When?

28:52.689 --> 28:55.484
Why didn't you tell me?

28:55.567 --> 28:57.361
[salesman] Excuse me, sir!

28:58.654 --> 29:01.740
I can take care of my own issues,
so please don't worry.

29:02.324 --> 29:03.325
This one is good.

29:03.408 --> 29:05.535
-[cell phone beeps]
-[classmates muttering]

29:06.370 --> 29:09.331
-It's been over a minute.
-Okay, Ho-su.

29:09.414 --> 29:11.917
I'll call you again later.

29:13.043 --> 29:15.254
How long was that? How many seconds?

29:16.255 --> 29:18.757
Two minutes and 32 seconds.
Sorry, you failed!

29:18.840 --> 29:20.801
That's too bad.

29:20.884 --> 29:22.970
Who's next?

29:23.053 --> 29:24.930
-[water running]
-[music concludes]

29:29.518 --> 29:30.435
[door opens]

29:44.950 --> 29:48.287
Did you wipe with your hands or something?
Your skin's going to peel.

29:48.370 --> 29:49.871
[chuckles] Oh my.

29:49.955 --> 29:52.624
I know. I wasted too much water.

30:00.549 --> 30:03.176
Sometimes it feels like
they're someone else's kid.

30:04.845 --> 30:06.888
They act like they raised themselves.

30:07.431 --> 30:09.725
They don't even remember
who changed their dirty diapers

30:09.808 --> 30:12.311
and who'd tell them,
"Don't worry. I'll take care of it."

30:12.394 --> 30:16.523
Hey, just take it as the price
of raising a brilliant kid.

30:16.606 --> 30:19.151
Better than having one
who can't take care of herself.

30:21.111 --> 30:22.571
[water running]

30:22.654 --> 30:24.823
[soft pensive music playing]

30:26.033 --> 30:28.535
[classmates chattering]

30:31.079 --> 30:32.414
We're leaving in five minutes.

30:37.502 --> 30:41.089
The child you gave birth to
doesn't feel like yours?

30:41.173 --> 30:43.425
I don't think I can relate.

30:49.306 --> 30:52.017
It's funny how you act so cold
to your real one.

30:52.100 --> 30:53.101
[music fades]

30:53.185 --> 30:55.729
-Pardon?
-To your real mom, I mean.

30:55.812 --> 30:59.941
I overheard, and it sounded like
you just told her that you'd quit.

31:01.318 --> 31:02.444
She…

31:03.612 --> 31:05.405
worries about me a lot.

31:08.200 --> 31:12.662
Letting your parents worry a little
is part of being a good son.

31:13.955 --> 31:14.956
To me,

31:16.291 --> 31:19.795
being a good son means
moving on and letting her have her life.

31:20.295 --> 31:22.589
Who am I to judge

31:22.672 --> 31:25.842
a parent-child relationship
based on something I just overheard?

31:26.802 --> 31:28.470
Sorry about earlier.

31:29.137 --> 31:32.224
For lying and saying you were my client
when you were right there with me.

31:32.307 --> 31:35.644
Instead of lying,
why don't we make it a reality?

31:36.144 --> 31:38.188
What do you mean?

31:40.982 --> 31:42.651
[gentle music playing]

31:43.276 --> 31:44.569
Pardon?

31:44.653 --> 31:48.115
So you're saying that
starting now, he's officially your…

31:48.198 --> 31:50.158
Legal representative.

31:52.828 --> 31:56.415
I'll go to the meeting
since I already promised I would.

31:56.498 --> 31:59.793
But from now on, handle all those
annoying issues through your friend.

31:59.876 --> 32:03.004
-[exhales] Ms. Ro-sa.
-Oh, and here.

32:04.589 --> 32:07.175
-What's all this?
-The documents I need before the meeting.

32:07.259 --> 32:08.718
What?

32:08.802 --> 32:12.180
We should at least know
the company's terms for negotiations.

32:12.264 --> 32:15.308
Send me the purchase proposal
and the business plan first,

32:15.392 --> 32:17.102
-and if possible…
-Hey.

32:18.854 --> 32:21.982
Why are you making this a big deal?
We're friends.

32:22.649 --> 32:24.609
Work is work, and friends are friends.

32:25.193 --> 32:26.528
Send them by Monday.

32:28.071 --> 32:30.157
[both exhale]

32:30.699 --> 32:31.658
[music concludes]

32:31.741 --> 32:34.327
-I'll head out first.
-I'll finish up and head home too.

32:34.411 --> 32:35.954
-Good work today.
-Thanks.

32:43.211 --> 32:44.880
WONGEUN LAW FIRM

32:48.425 --> 32:49.634
Hey!

32:49.718 --> 32:52.971
I gave you work because I felt bad.
How could you give me more work?

32:53.054 --> 32:54.639
It's not me.

32:54.723 --> 32:58.226
Your company did
an unacceptably sloppy job.

32:58.310 --> 32:59.895
-[cell phone buzzing]
-Jeez.

33:00.687 --> 33:02.063
Let me take this call.

33:03.648 --> 33:05.066
Hey, Ji-yun.

33:05.150 --> 33:06.902
Hi, Ho-su. [chuckles]

33:07.819 --> 33:10.113
Thanks to you, the interview went well.

33:10.197 --> 33:11.114
[chuckles]

33:11.198 --> 33:14.284
It's all because of you.
You even made the reservation for me.

33:15.952 --> 33:17.662
Are you at the office?

33:18.580 --> 33:21.500
If you are, I thought I'd stop by
for a quick chat.

33:22.167 --> 33:24.002
Uh… I quit the firm.

33:25.962 --> 33:27.005
You quit?

33:28.131 --> 33:30.967
-Just like that?
-Yes, it just happened.

33:33.053 --> 33:34.262
This weekend?

33:34.930 --> 33:37.224
Is the reunion you mentioned
this weekend?

33:37.974 --> 33:38.934
[whispers] What reunion?

33:39.017 --> 33:40.310
Okay.

33:40.977 --> 33:44.105
Did you tell Mi-rae?

33:44.731 --> 33:45.815
Uh…

33:46.650 --> 33:49.653
No, I didn't tell her on purpose.

33:50.320 --> 33:52.322
What do you mean by "on purpose"?

33:53.156 --> 33:55.158
I guess you don't know,

33:55.242 --> 33:59.204
but Mi-rae doesn't really socialize
since giving up on the civil service exam.

33:59.287 --> 34:01.122
Everyone knows how hard she worked.

34:01.206 --> 34:03.833
It must be hard for her
to have people see how she is now.

34:03.917 --> 34:05.377
What's wrong with how she is now?

34:05.460 --> 34:07.837
I don't mean she's in a bad place.

34:07.921 --> 34:11.633
From her perspective,
she probably feels like she settled.

34:11.716 --> 34:14.135
I think she feels awkward
about meeting everyone.

34:15.095 --> 34:19.099
Ji-yun, I appreciate the thought,
but I'll be there too.

34:19.182 --> 34:20.141
What?

34:20.559 --> 34:21.935
[intriguing quirky music playing]

34:22.018 --> 34:24.563
I'll bring Ho-su with me. See you there.

34:25.230 --> 34:26.314
[cell phone beeps]

34:26.398 --> 34:29.401
What was that? Are you going?

34:29.484 --> 34:30.610
Of course I am.

34:30.694 --> 34:33.822
They're painting me as a social recluse
who failed the civil service exam.

34:33.905 --> 34:35.490
But you don't have to…

34:35.574 --> 34:38.034
Why would you take me?

34:38.118 --> 34:39.202
And you…

34:39.953 --> 34:41.705
Come looking sharp.

34:41.788 --> 34:44.332
Otherwise,
they'll gossip about you forever.

34:44.416 --> 34:46.001
Get your hair done too.

34:49.045 --> 34:50.088
[Ho-su] What's with you?

34:50.171 --> 34:53.550
Since when do you care about that stuff?
If you don't want to go, then don't.

34:53.633 --> 34:55.343
Why give them the satisfaction?

34:55.427 --> 34:57.721
If I don't go,
they'll say whatever they want.

34:57.804 --> 34:59.723
"Mi-rae this" and "Mi-rae that."

34:59.806 --> 35:02.559
I'm not letting that happen.
I'm going, no matter what.

35:05.937 --> 35:07.272
What's up with her?

35:10.609 --> 35:12.527
FALL RISK
BED REST ONLY

35:16.031 --> 35:17.907
I wondered where that went.
Did you wash it?

35:17.991 --> 35:19.451
Yes, I did.

35:19.534 --> 35:21.536
Grandma kept looking for it.

35:21.620 --> 35:23.747
It gets pretty chilly at night these days.

35:23.830 --> 35:25.457
I see.

35:25.540 --> 35:26.458
[caregiver 1] Mi-ji.

35:26.541 --> 35:28.501
It's about time
you gave Grandma a haircut.

35:28.585 --> 35:30.378
Okay… What?

35:31.504 --> 35:32.672
Me?

35:33.256 --> 35:34.924
You've always done it yourself.

35:35.008 --> 35:37.469
Time to reopen "Mi-ji's salon,"
don't you think?

35:37.552 --> 35:38.595
[caregiver 2] That's right.

35:38.678 --> 35:41.681
At this pace, they'll turn
into gray-haired witches.

35:41.765 --> 35:44.726
-[chuckles]
-I'll see… what I can do.

35:44.809 --> 35:47.020
How did Grandma's skills

35:47.103 --> 35:49.564
skip her daughter
and land on her granddaughter?

35:49.648 --> 35:50.774
That's amazing.

35:50.857 --> 35:54.194
They say talent skips a generation.

35:54.277 --> 35:57.197
Is your sister good with hair too?

35:57.947 --> 36:00.158
No, she's not really good with her hands.

36:00.241 --> 36:03.328
It's not about skill.
She just doesn't care.

36:03.411 --> 36:06.247
-[melancholic music playing]
-There's always one in every family.

36:06.331 --> 36:09.751
They think giving money is enough
and wash their hands of everything else.

36:09.834 --> 36:12.629
She's probably just busy making money.

36:12.712 --> 36:14.172
Kids like Mi-ji are rare.

36:14.255 --> 36:18.301
Still, she hasn't shown her face once
since I've been here.

36:18.385 --> 36:19.969
Grandma's going to forget her face.

36:20.053 --> 36:21.930
[chuckles] How could she forget?

36:22.013 --> 36:25.684
-She looks just like Mi-ji.
-[caregiver 1] Good point.

36:25.767 --> 36:27.936
[caregivers giggle]

36:28.019 --> 36:29.813
Here, have these while you work.

36:29.896 --> 36:31.481
-[nurse] Wow.
-They're still a bit tart.

36:31.564 --> 36:33.525
But they'll wake you up!

36:33.608 --> 36:36.444
-Thank you.
-Please, try some.

36:36.528 --> 36:38.405
By the way, ma'am,

36:38.488 --> 36:41.241
have you had a chance to check
this month's payment?

36:41.908 --> 36:43.243
What about it?

36:43.993 --> 36:45.537
Well…

36:45.620 --> 36:49.290
Some things haven't been paid for yet.

36:49.374 --> 36:52.168
The caregiver fee and the meals.

36:53.461 --> 36:55.380
That can't be right.

36:56.131 --> 36:58.883
Wasn't it transferred under "Yu Mi-rae"?

36:58.967 --> 37:01.928
There's nothing on record
for this month yet.

37:02.011 --> 37:03.263
Oh dear.

37:05.098 --> 37:07.517
Maybe she forgot because she's so busy.

37:07.600 --> 37:09.018
I'll look into it.

37:15.150 --> 37:16.484
What the…

37:26.453 --> 37:27.996
[student 1]
So what happens to Mi-ji now?

37:28.079 --> 37:30.874
[student 2] What do you mean?
She's done for. She didn't get into HNU.

37:30.957 --> 37:32.876
[student 3] Life really is unpredictable.

37:32.959 --> 37:35.003
-What's she going to do now?
-[student 1] What else?

37:35.086 --> 37:36.504
She should marry Gyeong-gu.

37:36.588 --> 37:37.797
[student 3] That's not so bad.

37:37.881 --> 37:39.758
-[student 2] Come on!
-[student 3] It's possible.

37:39.841 --> 37:41.259
[student 2] Like in a romance comic!

37:41.342 --> 37:43.261
[student 3] It's not like
one of them is settling.

37:43.344 --> 37:44.304
[student 2] That's harsh!

37:44.387 --> 37:46.639
[student 3] Elementary school sweethearts
getting married.

37:46.723 --> 37:49.058
-[student 2] This is pure romance.
-[student 3] Seriously.

37:49.142 --> 37:51.478
[suspenseful music playing]

37:51.561 --> 37:52.562
[breathes deeply]

37:53.354 --> 37:54.856
Yesterday is over.

37:55.523 --> 37:57.692
Tomorrow is yet to come. Today is.…

37:57.776 --> 37:59.611
-[door opens]
-[music stops abruptly]

38:00.487 --> 38:01.863
[man] Mi-ji?

38:01.946 --> 38:03.323
Or is it Mi-rae?

38:05.492 --> 38:07.118
-Mi-rae.
-[chuckles]

38:07.786 --> 38:09.162
Long time no see, Mi-rae.

38:09.245 --> 38:12.540
[students chanting]
Choi Seung-hyeon! Choi Seung-hyeon!

38:12.624 --> 38:15.210
Choi Seung-hyeon! Choi Seung-hyeon!

38:15.293 --> 38:17.670
-[students cheering]
-[pensive music playing]

38:19.172 --> 38:21.007
Does he ever pass the ball?

38:21.090 --> 38:22.926
[student] That's insane. He's on fire!

38:23.009 --> 38:26.012
-[classmate 1] Really, what's the secret?
-[classmate 2] Hey there!

38:26.095 --> 38:27.680
-[group chuckles]
-He looks amazing.

38:27.764 --> 38:29.140
[music fades]

38:30.225 --> 38:33.353
Take a guess.
Is she Mi-ji or Mi-rae?

38:33.436 --> 38:35.355
-[door closes]
-[footsteps approaching]

38:36.272 --> 38:37.857
[Ji-yun] Mi-rae's here.

38:37.941 --> 38:40.276
Come on, Ji-yun. What a buzzkill.

38:40.360 --> 38:41.486
[classmate 2] It's Mi-rae.

38:41.569 --> 38:44.447
It's been ages. We never get to see you.

38:45.365 --> 38:48.201
It's been crazy at the office.

38:48.284 --> 38:50.453
Right, you work at the KFMC.

38:50.537 --> 38:51.913
No wonder you're so busy.

38:51.996 --> 38:54.290
Still, you should've shown up
for weddings and stuff.

38:54.374 --> 38:56.042
You missed
our wedding invitation gathering.

38:56.125 --> 38:57.210
Are you two getting married?

38:57.293 --> 38:59.879
-[hesitates, chuckles]
-Come on, we've got a two-year-old.

38:59.963 --> 39:02.090
Ji-yun, you didn't tell Mi-rae about us?

39:02.173 --> 39:03.925
I did tell her.

39:04.008 --> 39:05.718
I told you. You probably forgot.

39:05.802 --> 39:10.181
If you ask me, Mi-rae's the only one
who traveled through time.

39:10.265 --> 39:11.432
[group laughs]

39:11.516 --> 39:13.101
Let's sit. Have we ordered yet?

39:13.184 --> 39:14.602
[classmate 2] Yes, all done.

39:15.645 --> 39:17.188
What's the best thing on the menu?

39:17.272 --> 39:18.857
[classmate 2] It really has been a while.

39:18.940 --> 39:19.983
[mutters, chuckles]

39:20.065 --> 39:21.025
HOW TO CUT GRANDMA'S HAIR

39:25.321 --> 39:26.364
[sighs]

39:26.447 --> 39:30.076
[Ok-hui] Oh my. This is driving me crazy.

39:33.413 --> 39:35.665
Seriously, what do I do?

39:35.748 --> 39:38.293
I feel so hopeless. [sighs]

39:40.837 --> 39:43.172
What is it? What's wrong?

39:46.384 --> 39:47.510
[sighs]

39:47.594 --> 39:49.971
Is something going on with Mi-rae?

39:51.264 --> 39:52.682
What do you mean?

39:54.350 --> 39:57.562
I mean, even if she never calls,

39:58.771 --> 40:01.608
she always pays
the hospital bills right on time.

40:02.609 --> 40:04.861
Do you think she's having money problems?

40:06.779 --> 40:08.364
I'll cover it this time.

40:10.867 --> 40:13.953
Goodness, with what money?

40:14.495 --> 40:16.623
I've been working on the farm.
I'll pay you in cash.

40:16.706 --> 40:19.292
Don't waste your money.

40:19.375 --> 40:20.752
Just save it.

40:20.835 --> 40:21.961
[sighs]

40:22.045 --> 40:24.047
I make more per hour than Mi-rae.

40:24.130 --> 40:25.673
I'll save what's left--

40:25.757 --> 40:27.091
Jeez!

40:27.675 --> 40:28.968
Just save it.

40:35.224 --> 40:37.310
Is it okay to use Mi-rae's money, then?

40:37.936 --> 40:40.104
You think you and Mi-rae are the same?

40:41.564 --> 40:42.482
What's so different?

40:42.565 --> 40:44.525
What do you think? I mean…

40:44.609 --> 40:46.903
[melancholic music playing]

40:50.907 --> 40:51.866
[door opens]

40:58.289 --> 40:59.832
[sighs]

40:59.916 --> 41:01.125
[group] Cheers!

41:01.209 --> 41:04.003
[classmate 1] Remember when Seung-hyeon
did the speech at graduation?

41:04.087 --> 41:07.465
Girls from other schools and lower grades
were bawling their eyes out.

41:07.548 --> 41:09.759
Stop. That's ancient history.

41:09.842 --> 41:11.386
-[classmate 1] Seriously.
-[door opens]

41:11.469 --> 41:12.804
[music concludes]

41:12.887 --> 41:13.930
Ho-su, you made it.

41:14.013 --> 41:15.056
[classmate 1] Hey, Ho-su!

41:15.139 --> 41:16.432
Long time no see.

41:17.183 --> 41:19.060
-You're looking good.
-[classmate 2] So handsome.

41:19.143 --> 41:21.354
-[classmate 3] He is.
-[classmates muttering]

41:23.898 --> 41:25.066
[mouths] You're late.

41:26.859 --> 41:28.736
[classmate] I heard you're a lawyer now.

41:28.820 --> 41:30.738
He's the only lawyer
from our class, right?

41:30.822 --> 41:34.450
That's wild.
I've never met a real lawyer before.

41:34.534 --> 41:36.244
[group chuckles]

41:36.327 --> 41:37.996
Where did you do your military service?

41:38.079 --> 41:40.790
Do lawyers get assigned
to special roles like army doctors?

41:40.873 --> 41:42.291
I'm not sure.

41:42.375 --> 41:43.710
I was exempt.

41:44.419 --> 41:46.838
Shoot. Sorry, I forgot.

41:46.921 --> 41:49.257
[classmate 1] Wow, you're blessed, man.

41:49.340 --> 41:51.426
Ho-su, can I get your business card?

41:51.509 --> 41:53.177
-Gosh.
-Okay.

41:53.970 --> 41:55.263
I don't have…

41:55.346 --> 41:56.973
You know Wongeun Law Firm, right?

41:57.056 --> 41:59.058
-[classmate 3] Yes.
-Ho-su was there until recently.

41:59.142 --> 42:02.353
Wongeun? Isn't that
the top firm in Korea? [gasps]

42:02.437 --> 42:05.857
What's up with you two?
Since when have you two kept in touch?

42:05.940 --> 42:07.900
-Gosh!
-[classmate 4 exclaims playfully]

42:07.984 --> 42:11.362
Ho-su and Mi-rae…
I always knew you two would do well.

42:11.446 --> 42:12.572
Come on.

42:12.655 --> 42:15.283
They were the top two in the whole school.
We all knew it.

42:15.366 --> 42:16.242
[both chuckle]

42:16.325 --> 42:20.455
Turns out Duson High
has some pretty successful alumni.

42:20.538 --> 42:22.957
A lawyer,
and a public corporation employee.

42:23.041 --> 42:25.626
I honestly thought Seung-hyeon
would be the most successful.

42:25.710 --> 42:27.253
[whispers] Hey.

42:27.336 --> 42:29.964
He's way too good-looking
to just be a store clerk.

42:30.048 --> 42:32.341
I thought he'd be
a TV personality or something.

42:32.425 --> 42:34.427
He's not just a clerk. He's a manager.

42:34.510 --> 42:35.553
I know.

42:35.636 --> 42:38.973
[laughs] Sorry, she's drunk.

42:39.057 --> 42:41.517
Cut her some slack.
She used to be your fan club president.

42:41.601 --> 42:44.145
Thanks for seeing me in such a good light.

42:45.104 --> 42:48.524
But Mi-ji was
the most likely to succeed, right?

42:48.608 --> 42:51.194
-That's true.
-[classmate 3] I know.

42:51.277 --> 42:53.905
[Ji-yun] What's she doing these days
after quitting track and field?

42:53.988 --> 42:57.116
I saw her in Duson-ri the other day.
She was moving some stuff at the mart.

42:57.200 --> 42:59.243
-[classmate 3] What?
-My mom said she's a janitor.

42:59.327 --> 43:01.579
-[pensive music playing]
-[classmate 2] Wait, a janitor?

43:01.662 --> 43:04.332
[student 1] What do you mean?
She's done for. She didn't get into HNU.

43:04.415 --> 43:06.959
-[student 2] She should marry Gyeong-gu.
-[student 1] That's harsh!

43:07.043 --> 43:08.503
Like in a romance comic!

43:08.586 --> 43:10.505
[student 2]
It's not like one of them is settling.

43:10.588 --> 43:12.423
[echoing overlapping chatter and laughter]

43:12.507 --> 43:14.592
[Ji-yun] Don't ask me.
Her twin is sitting next to you.

43:14.675 --> 43:15.760
[classmate 2] Fair point.

43:15.843 --> 43:17.595
[Ji-yun] Mi-rae, how's Mi-ji doing?

43:17.678 --> 43:19.097
[classmate 4]
Why would you ask that?

43:19.180 --> 43:21.265
[classmate 1]
Mi-rae, you must have it so hard.

43:21.349 --> 43:23.643
-[music builds]
-Why are we talking…

43:24.977 --> 43:26.896
-[music concludes]
-…behind her back?

43:32.068 --> 43:33.444
[chuckles nervously]

43:33.528 --> 43:37.198
Ho-su still goes from zero
to a hundred in no time.

43:37.281 --> 43:38.616
Just like the old days.

43:39.659 --> 43:41.285
But he's right.

43:41.369 --> 43:43.371
Mi-rae's right here too.

43:44.247 --> 43:45.998
[classmates chuckle nervously]

43:46.082 --> 43:48.251
[Seung-hyeon] Is the wedding
really happening this time?

43:48.334 --> 43:50.294
-[classmate 2] Of course!
-[classmate 4] Definitely.

43:50.378 --> 43:52.672
[Seung-hyeon] You said that last time,
but it didn't happen.

43:52.755 --> 43:55.216
-[classmate 2] This time we have to do it.
-[Seung-hyeon] Really?

43:55.299 --> 43:58.302
-[classmate 2] You better come.
-[Seung-hyeon] I will. [laughs]

44:00.471 --> 44:03.099
Ho-su! You should come to the wedding too.

44:03.182 --> 44:04.892
[Ho-su] Okay.
It's a bit late, but congrats.

44:04.976 --> 44:06.269
[Mi-ji] Yes, congratulations.

44:06.352 --> 44:08.354
-[classmate 1] Bye.
-[Mi-ji] See you.

44:08.437 --> 44:09.814
Ho-su, are you leaving?

44:09.897 --> 44:11.482
-I'll join you then.
-Hey, traitor!

44:11.566 --> 44:14.485
You got us all together.
You're staying till the end.

44:14.569 --> 44:16.028
Bye. I'll call you.

44:16.112 --> 44:17.780
[classmate 2] Who's up for karaoke?

44:17.864 --> 44:18.739
Mi-rae.

44:20.741 --> 44:23.953
I just realized
I don't have your number.

44:25.705 --> 44:26.706
Ah…

44:27.832 --> 44:29.000
Okay.

44:31.961 --> 44:33.713
-Here.
-[Seung-hyeon in English] Thank you.

44:34.922 --> 44:37.300
[in Korean]
I'll contact you before the wedding.

44:37.383 --> 44:39.552
If you're going, then let's go together.

44:39.635 --> 44:40.761
All right.

44:43.264 --> 44:44.891
Would you like to come with us?

44:47.518 --> 44:49.061
Do you want me to?

44:50.813 --> 44:52.815
[laughs] I'll get going.

44:52.899 --> 44:55.026
-You two take care.
-Okay.

45:02.408 --> 45:03.826
How are you getting home?

45:05.244 --> 45:06.329
No idea.

45:09.207 --> 45:10.499
Are you mad?

45:11.918 --> 45:13.044
Why would I be?

45:13.628 --> 45:15.046
How should I know?

45:16.505 --> 45:20.301
You've barely said a word,
and you don't seem so happy.

45:20.885 --> 45:22.595
What's there to be happy about?

45:23.137 --> 45:24.805
It wasn't exactly a fun gathering.

45:24.889 --> 45:26.557
Then why did you even come?

45:28.768 --> 45:30.519
No, seriously.

45:31.270 --> 45:34.273
You're not the type to show up
just because I asked you to.

45:37.026 --> 45:38.569
Why did you come?

45:38.653 --> 45:39.570
Me?

45:40.112 --> 45:42.406
-I've already told you.
-[Ho-su] Right.

45:42.490 --> 45:44.992
You said you hate it
when people gossip about you.

45:45.952 --> 45:48.037
Then why were you so quiet earlier?

45:48.120 --> 45:49.038
What?

45:49.121 --> 45:52.041
You can't stand people talking about you
behind your back,

45:52.124 --> 45:55.127
but you're fine with them
talking about Mi-ji right in front of you?

45:55.211 --> 45:57.838
[soft pensive music playing]

46:00.299 --> 46:01.425
I'll get going.

46:05.638 --> 46:06.722
[exhales]

46:13.938 --> 46:15.731
[soft pensive music continues]

46:32.581 --> 46:34.375
[music fades]

46:34.458 --> 46:36.085
[cell phone buzzing]

46:40.339 --> 46:41.340
[Mi-ji] Hello.

46:41.424 --> 46:43.759
Why weren't you answering your phone?

46:43.843 --> 46:46.470
[Mi-ji] Sorry, I was out,
so I didn't notice.

46:46.554 --> 46:47.763
What's up?

46:47.847 --> 46:50.141
[sighs] You've been paid, right?

46:51.892 --> 46:54.020
I forgot to mention the hospital bill.

46:54.437 --> 46:56.439
I texted you my bank account info.

46:56.522 --> 46:58.524
Transfer the money
and keep the rest for yourself.

46:58.607 --> 47:02.194
No thanks. It's your paycheck.

47:02.278 --> 47:04.071
[Mi-rae] You're the one who went to work.

47:04.155 --> 47:06.949
Anyway, come down on Friday.

47:07.033 --> 47:08.492
Grandma needs a haircut.

47:09.702 --> 47:10.828
Oh…

47:10.911 --> 47:12.955
Can't it be another day?

47:13.039 --> 47:15.541
Mom's not coming home on Friday night.

47:15.624 --> 47:17.710
You should come when she's not around.

47:17.793 --> 47:19.503
Any other day works for me.

47:19.587 --> 47:22.173
I have something on Friday.

47:22.256 --> 47:23.841
Something? Like what?

47:24.383 --> 47:25.426
Well…

47:26.010 --> 47:28.637
There's this really important meeting
at work.

47:28.721 --> 47:30.556
I have to be there.

47:30.639 --> 47:32.099
[Mi-rae sighs] Just come down.

47:32.183 --> 47:33.684
They don't need me anyway.

47:33.768 --> 47:36.479
[Mi-ji] Still,
I should do what the company asks…

47:36.562 --> 47:39.899
Do what? I told you to just sit tight.

47:39.982 --> 47:43.277
Come on.
I can't just sit there and do nothing.

47:44.278 --> 47:45.613
Gosh.

47:46.197 --> 47:48.824
I'll make time and come later.

47:48.908 --> 47:51.452
[scoffs] You're unbelievable.

47:51.535 --> 47:53.496
So work comes before Grandma now?

47:54.080 --> 47:56.665
-That's a stretch.
-What is?

47:56.749 --> 47:58.834
It's what you always said to me.

47:58.918 --> 48:00.669
It's not the same for me.

48:00.753 --> 48:02.797
And I'm not doing this for myself.

48:02.880 --> 48:05.091
-It's all for you--
-What's so different?

48:05.174 --> 48:07.426
I wasn't doing it for myself either.

48:07.510 --> 48:09.512
[pensive music playing]

48:10.971 --> 48:14.392
Anyway, I really can't make it on Friday.

48:14.475 --> 48:15.893
What am I supposed to…

48:16.936 --> 48:19.313
Should I tell Mom
to change her plans for you?

48:19.397 --> 48:21.482
What's with the attitude?

48:21.565 --> 48:22.525
[Mi-rae] Forget it.

48:22.608 --> 48:24.443
I'll handle the haircut
and everything else.

48:24.527 --> 48:25.736
Just send the money.

48:25.820 --> 48:28.406
Is it that much of a burden
to take care of Grandma for me?

48:28.489 --> 48:31.784
If it is, then don't do it!
That's what you always told me.

48:34.870 --> 48:38.749
Is it as easy as you thought,
just sending money from Seoul?

48:39.250 --> 48:41.043
-What?
-Transfer the money now.

48:41.710 --> 48:42.586
[Mi-ji] Hey.

48:42.670 --> 48:43.963
[cell phone beeps, thuds]

48:46.590 --> 48:47.716
[sighs]

48:54.098 --> 48:55.558
CALL ENDED

48:55.641 --> 48:57.935
[sighs] She's freaking mean.

48:58.018 --> 48:59.478
[pensive music continues]

49:10.781 --> 49:14.243
-[music fades]
-[cell phone chiming]

49:24.253 --> 49:25.754
NICE SEEING YOU
SEE YOU AT THE WEDDING!

49:31.844 --> 49:34.263
[tender quirky music playing]

49:35.139 --> 49:36.599
Just sip at your own pace.

49:37.683 --> 49:39.477
-[chuckles] Thanks.
-[chuckles]

49:42.980 --> 49:44.315
[Mi-ji] Are you mad?

49:44.857 --> 49:46.442
What's there to be happy about?

49:47.026 --> 49:48.736
It wasn't exactly a fun gathering.

49:49.528 --> 49:51.280
Then why did you even come?

49:55.451 --> 49:56.494
[cell phone clunks]

50:03.751 --> 50:06.795
[Secretary Hwang] When you see her,
your feelings are all over the place,

50:06.879 --> 50:09.507
and you end up doing whatever she wants.

50:09.590 --> 50:13.928
Do you know what you call this
neuropsychiatric symptom?

50:14.470 --> 50:15.638
[sighs]

50:19.683 --> 50:21.810
[music concludes]

50:21.894 --> 50:23.229
[jogging footsteps]

50:23.896 --> 50:27.483
I've finally cleared out
all of last year's produce!

50:27.566 --> 50:28.776
What's all this?

50:29.652 --> 50:32.613
Some boxes and shipping labels.

50:32.696 --> 50:34.281
-For you to send out.
-Oh.

50:34.365 --> 50:36.784
I don't have anyone to send them to.

50:36.867 --> 50:38.202
You haven't sent any to Seoul yet.

50:38.285 --> 50:40.704
Send some to your twin
to share with her friends.

50:42.498 --> 50:45.000
She has no one
to share them with in Seoul.

50:45.084 --> 50:46.627
That can't be right.

50:46.710 --> 50:51.090
Strawberries aren't a big deal here,
but in Seoul, you have to pay for them.

50:51.173 --> 50:55.094
Even if I send these, they'll just spoil.
There's no one to share them with.

50:55.177 --> 50:57.805
How can there be no one?
Seoul is not a deserted island.

50:58.639 --> 51:00.182
She only cares about herself.

51:00.683 --> 51:01.725
[soft music playing]

51:01.809 --> 51:04.853
Only her problems matter,
and only her struggles count.

51:04.937 --> 51:06.313
That's why she has no one.

51:07.606 --> 51:09.400
Still, she can have some strawberries.

51:10.776 --> 51:13.195
Do whatever you want. They're yours.

51:22.621 --> 51:24.415
PARCEL SHIPPING FORM

51:24.498 --> 51:26.792
RECIPIENT ADDRESS

51:30.129 --> 51:31.672
[Bun-hong] Mi-ji.

51:31.755 --> 51:32.923
Hello.

51:33.007 --> 51:34.717
-[music fades]
-[Bun-hong] Is your mom home?

51:34.800 --> 51:38.846
She said she's staying over
at a friend's tonight.

51:39.513 --> 51:40.848
Mm…

51:41.432 --> 51:43.934
I never seem to catch your mom
at the right time.

51:44.018 --> 51:45.477
I wanted to talk to her.

51:46.186 --> 51:47.896
What's with all these strawberries?

51:47.980 --> 51:51.317
I got them from work. Would you like some?

51:52.318 --> 51:55.779
They're organic, but they're a bit tart.

51:55.863 --> 51:56.780
Mm!

51:57.740 --> 51:58.866
You're right.

51:59.450 --> 52:04.705
The tart, ugly ones like these
are perfect for jam.

52:07.458 --> 52:10.419
Mi-ji, do you want to make
strawberry jam with me?

52:11.295 --> 52:12.254
Sorry?

52:13.172 --> 52:15.674
[rain pattering]

52:28.937 --> 52:32.066
[grunting]

52:42.368 --> 52:44.953
-[yelps]
-[ominous music playing]

52:45.037 --> 52:49.083
[groaning]

52:49.917 --> 52:51.919
[breathing heavily]

52:52.002 --> 52:53.629
[cell phone buzzing]

52:53.712 --> 52:54.755
[grunts]

52:59.343 --> 53:01.220
For God's sake.

53:03.514 --> 53:05.516
[dial tone ringing]

53:05.599 --> 53:07.351
[music fades]

53:07.434 --> 53:10.646
[automated voice] The person
you are trying to reach is not available.

53:10.729 --> 53:13.315
-Please try again later.
-She's not answering.

53:13.399 --> 53:14.650
[door opens]

53:15.943 --> 53:17.027
Oh…

53:17.653 --> 53:20.239
Still setting up? Where is the landowner?

53:20.864 --> 53:24.159
She should be on her way,
but I can't reach her.

53:25.452 --> 53:26.578
You can't reach her?

53:27.996 --> 53:30.290
Is she ghosting you or something?

53:30.374 --> 53:32.835
I'll ask her representative
who was supposed to come.

53:32.918 --> 53:34.753
[cell phone buzzing]

53:37.005 --> 53:38.966
-Hello.
-You're on your way, right?

53:39.049 --> 53:40.759
And you're with Ms. Ro-sa?

53:41.844 --> 53:44.471
No, we agreed to meet at your office.

53:44.555 --> 53:45.973
-What?
-[suspenseful music playing]

53:46.056 --> 53:48.142
When was the last time
you spoke with her?

53:48.809 --> 53:50.436
We spoke last night.

53:51.311 --> 53:52.938
I haven't called her today.

53:53.021 --> 53:54.064
[breathes sharply]

53:54.148 --> 53:56.900
Did she say anything unusual last night?

53:56.984 --> 53:59.027
She just said, "See you at the meeting."

53:59.778 --> 54:02.614
Why? Is she not answering?
Should I go to her place?

54:03.157 --> 54:06.618
No, it's fine.
Just come to the office for now.

54:06.702 --> 54:08.620
Once I finish setting up the meeting room…

54:08.704 --> 54:10.038
Wait, never mind.

54:10.122 --> 54:11.790
I'll just go there myself.

54:11.874 --> 54:13.000
[employee] I'll do it.

54:13.709 --> 54:14.752
[Mi-ji] Pardon?

54:14.835 --> 54:18.088
I'll finish getting things ready here.
You go check on her.

54:18.172 --> 54:19.923
-Oh…
-[Ho-su] What's going on?

54:20.007 --> 54:22.885
Oh… Nothing. I'll go.

54:22.968 --> 54:24.344
-[cell phone beeps]
-Mi-rae.

54:27.306 --> 54:30.476
Then I'll leave it to you. Thank you.

54:37.399 --> 54:39.026
-Ma'am!
-[knocking on door]

54:39.109 --> 54:40.444
[music fades]

54:40.527 --> 54:41.695
Ma'am!

54:42.362 --> 54:43.655
Are you home?

54:44.198 --> 54:45.199
[sighs]

54:46.366 --> 54:49.912
If she's not home,
where could she possibly be?

54:49.995 --> 54:51.330
[dial tone ringing]

54:51.413 --> 54:52.623
Ms. Ro-sa!

54:53.957 --> 54:54.875
Oh!

54:56.460 --> 54:58.712
-Ma'am?
-[ringing continues]

54:58.796 --> 55:01.131
[Ro-sa groaning] Oh my goodness.

55:05.719 --> 55:06.762
[mumbling] Oh gosh.

55:06.845 --> 55:08.597
-[gasps]
-[suspenseful music playing]

55:08.680 --> 55:10.098
[loud clatter]

55:17.439 --> 55:18.941
[young Mi-ji echoing] Grandma!

55:19.858 --> 55:21.985
-Ms. Ro-sa!
-Gosh.

55:22.861 --> 55:26.698
I thought I was going to
starve to death here all alone.

55:26.782 --> 55:27.825
[groans]

55:27.908 --> 55:30.160
It's just a minor sprain in my back.

55:30.786 --> 55:31.995
Call 911.

55:32.079 --> 55:34.039
[whimpering]

55:34.122 --> 55:36.792
[hyperventilating]

55:42.422 --> 55:43.966
[Mi-ji gasping]

55:44.049 --> 55:47.177
Hey. What's going on?

55:47.886 --> 55:49.680
-[Ro-sa groaning]
-[continues gasping]

55:49.763 --> 55:52.307
[Ro-sa] What's wrong?

55:52.391 --> 55:54.601
-Stay with me, okay?
-[fast knocking on door]

55:55.352 --> 55:56.478
Ma'am?

55:56.562 --> 55:59.189
-[Mi-ji gasping]
-[Ro-sa] Ho-su? Here!

55:59.273 --> 56:01.358
Over here!

56:01.441 --> 56:03.861
-Go get a plastic bag!
-Ma'am!

56:03.944 --> 56:05.779
-Put a bag over her mouth.
-[Ho-su] Okay.

56:05.863 --> 56:08.740
-All right.
-Go get a bag. Hurry!

56:08.824 --> 56:12.119
-Stay with me!
-[gasping]

56:12.202 --> 56:13.620
[Ho-su] Mi-rae, here!

56:13.704 --> 56:14.955
What's going on?

56:15.038 --> 56:17.791
-[Mi-ji groaning]
-[Ho-su] Calm down and breathe.

56:18.500 --> 56:20.711
[music concludes]

56:22.629 --> 56:26.508
[nurse over intercom] Attention, patients
and guardians in the emergency room…

56:27.551 --> 56:28.760
[doors whirring open]

56:35.309 --> 56:38.896
[gasps] Any word on the CT scan?

56:38.979 --> 56:40.439
Is it her brain?

56:40.522 --> 56:43.650
There's nothing serious on the scan.
Just a minor back injury.

56:43.734 --> 56:44.860
[sighs]

56:44.943 --> 56:47.571
[Ho-su] They'll keep an eye on her
until tomorrow, just to be safe.

56:47.654 --> 56:49.197
[exhales heavily]

56:51.158 --> 56:52.242
Are you okay?

56:52.951 --> 56:54.244
Still not feeling well?

56:54.328 --> 56:56.705
[sobs] It almost happened again.

56:57.623 --> 56:59.666
If it weren't for you, Ho-su…

57:02.586 --> 57:04.087
[sobs]

57:05.589 --> 57:07.507
Mi-ji, open the door.

57:08.258 --> 57:09.468
Open up.

57:09.551 --> 57:10.719
Yu Mi-ji!

57:12.846 --> 57:14.348
Yu Mi-ji!

57:14.431 --> 57:16.099
[panting]

57:19.394 --> 57:20.854
I can't take this anymore.

57:21.855 --> 57:25.067
Let's settle this
once and for all today.

57:40.666 --> 57:41.833
Get up.

57:42.960 --> 57:44.544
I said, "Get up."

57:44.628 --> 57:46.505
Why did you cut the phone line?

57:47.130 --> 57:48.340
Huh?

57:48.423 --> 57:49.508
Get up.

57:51.760 --> 57:54.012
You're not even going to
show your face anymore?

57:54.096 --> 57:55.514
Get up!

57:55.597 --> 57:57.766
Do you want to see me go crazy?

57:57.849 --> 57:59.351
Get up!

57:59.977 --> 58:02.104
Come on, I said get up!

58:04.314 --> 58:05.399
You…

58:06.316 --> 58:09.027
-[somber music playing]
-How long are you going to keep this up?

58:09.111 --> 58:11.530
You won't go outside,
you don't see anyone,

58:11.613 --> 58:13.782
and now you've cut the phone line too?

58:13.865 --> 58:16.702
You call this a home? It's a prison cell.

58:16.785 --> 58:19.287
Get up. Come on.

58:20.080 --> 58:22.207
Let's go out.

58:23.625 --> 58:26.628
It's been three years!

58:26.712 --> 58:29.923
You've done enough, and I've had enough!

58:30.549 --> 58:33.885
Just because you can't run anymore,
your life is over?

58:33.969 --> 58:38.432
How long are you going to waste your life
stuck in the past?

58:38.974 --> 58:41.226
Are you going to hide forever?

58:41.309 --> 58:43.770
[shouting]
What are you going to do with yourself?

58:44.646 --> 58:45.939
Since when do you care?

58:46.606 --> 58:48.775
[pants]

58:48.859 --> 58:50.027
What?

58:50.694 --> 58:53.196
Since when do you ever care about me?

58:53.280 --> 58:55.365
You don't give a damn what happens to me.

58:56.241 --> 58:57.951
Mi-ji.

58:58.035 --> 58:59.411
It's true, isn't it?

59:00.328 --> 59:03.123
You never paid any attention to me
before I started running.

59:03.206 --> 59:04.958
I can't run anymore.

59:05.042 --> 59:08.503
So just go back to worrying about Mi-rae,
like you always have.

59:08.587 --> 59:10.714
Do you hear yourself right now?

59:10.797 --> 59:13.133
To you, I've always been Mi-rae's add-on.

59:13.884 --> 59:16.178
So keep ignoring me like you always have.

59:16.261 --> 59:18.096
I'm just sitting here, dead quiet.

59:18.180 --> 59:20.390
So please leave me alone!

59:20.891 --> 59:23.351
So you're saying
all of this is my fault now?

59:23.894 --> 59:26.730
How far back are you going to trace this?

59:26.813 --> 59:29.357
What's next?
Will you blame me for giving birth to you?

59:29.441 --> 59:31.526
Yes, why did you even have me?

59:31.610 --> 59:33.528
You could've just had Mi-rae.

59:33.612 --> 59:35.238
You think so too, don't you?

59:35.322 --> 59:36.990
You brat!

59:37.074 --> 59:39.117
Did you really just say that?

59:39.201 --> 59:41.411
I can't believe you.

59:41.495 --> 59:45.499
How could you break
your mother's heart like that?

59:45.582 --> 59:47.626
-[Wol-sun] What are you doing?
-How could you do this?

59:47.709 --> 59:50.420
-You can't… Get up and come out.
-Calm down.

59:50.504 --> 59:53.757
-Come out!
-Stop! Come out!

59:56.343 --> 59:58.595
-[Ok-hui] Let go.
-[Wol-sun] Stay out of here.

01:00:02.390 --> 01:00:04.309
-[Ok-hui groans]
-Are you insane?

01:00:04.392 --> 01:00:06.394
Why are you going after her like that?

01:00:06.478 --> 01:00:09.689
If she won't come out,
maybe I have to make her!

01:00:09.773 --> 01:00:11.733
Give it time.

01:00:12.234 --> 01:00:14.277
You think this is something you can force?

01:00:14.361 --> 01:00:15.362
Jeez.

01:00:16.655 --> 01:00:18.406
This is all your fault!

01:00:18.990 --> 01:00:21.701
You coddled her too much
and turned her into a recluse.

01:00:21.785 --> 01:00:24.121
You were never like this with me as a kid,

01:00:24.204 --> 01:00:27.582
so why do you baby my kid and spoil her?

01:00:28.208 --> 01:00:29.209
Gosh.

01:00:29.292 --> 01:00:30.669
[Ok-hui sobs]

01:00:38.844 --> 01:00:39.970
[knocking on door]

01:00:40.595 --> 01:00:42.013
[music fades]

01:00:42.097 --> 01:00:43.181
[Wol-sun] Mi-ji.

01:00:45.016 --> 01:00:46.643
Grandma's coming in.

01:01:06.079 --> 01:01:08.790
Why are you sitting like that?
It must be suffocating.

01:01:10.834 --> 01:01:11.960
Look at me.

01:01:13.044 --> 01:01:14.045
Come on.

01:01:15.255 --> 01:01:16.590
[Mi-ji timidly] No.

01:01:16.673 --> 01:01:17.757
No?

01:01:18.425 --> 01:01:19.926
Then don't.

01:01:22.596 --> 01:01:24.890
Oh, my little cocoon.

01:01:24.973 --> 01:01:28.268
How big of a butterfly
are you trying to become?

01:01:29.352 --> 01:01:30.395
[Mi-ji] No.

01:01:31.771 --> 01:01:33.940
I'm not going to become anything.

01:01:34.608 --> 01:01:35.942
That's fine too.

01:01:36.985 --> 01:01:40.488
As long as you stay healthy, eat well,

01:01:40.572 --> 01:01:44.409
and keep Grandma company, that's enough.

01:01:46.036 --> 01:01:50.123
I have enough money to take care of you.

01:01:50.707 --> 01:01:52.042
I mean it.

01:02:01.509 --> 01:02:02.594
[sniffles]

01:02:02.677 --> 01:02:04.137
Grandma.

01:02:06.389 --> 01:02:08.600
There might be something wrong with me.

01:02:11.061 --> 01:02:13.730
I regret everything and worry so much…

01:02:15.023 --> 01:02:16.441
that I can't do anything.

01:02:17.692 --> 01:02:19.903
What's there to regret and worry about?

01:02:20.904 --> 01:02:23.573
Yesterday is over.

01:02:23.657 --> 01:02:25.951
Tomorrow is yet to come.

01:02:27.702 --> 01:02:28.870
I don't know.

01:02:30.163 --> 01:02:33.333
I know I should get out of here…

01:02:33.416 --> 01:02:35.085
-[sobs]
-[soft music playing]

01:02:35.168 --> 01:02:40.048
…but I don't want to go back
to being nothing again.

01:02:40.131 --> 01:02:43.718
I know that's the only place
I can go back to…

01:02:45.971 --> 01:02:47.847
but it feels so pathetic,

01:02:49.266 --> 01:02:50.767
and I'm sick of it.

01:02:51.726 --> 01:02:56.022
[sobbing]
I have all this life ahead of me,

01:02:58.066 --> 01:03:00.110
and I feel completely lost.

01:03:02.737 --> 01:03:04.114
Grandma.

01:03:05.282 --> 01:03:07.826
I feel like trash.

01:03:11.288 --> 01:03:15.208
If a deer runs away from a lion,

01:03:16.167 --> 01:03:17.752
does that make it trash?

01:03:19.004 --> 01:03:23.216
If a hermit crab hides
in fear of being eaten,

01:03:23.842 --> 01:03:24.968
is it a coward?

01:03:25.051 --> 01:03:27.637
They're all just trying to survive.

01:03:28.763 --> 01:03:31.433
You're hiding to survive too.

01:03:32.892 --> 01:03:36.521
No matter how pathetic or messy it looks,

01:03:36.604 --> 01:03:41.067
anything you do to survive is brave.

01:03:42.569 --> 01:03:43.862
[wails]

01:03:43.945 --> 01:03:46.031
Grandma.

01:03:51.244 --> 01:03:53.330
[crying loudly]

01:03:54.956 --> 01:03:56.875
It's okay, my dear.

01:03:56.958 --> 01:03:59.169
Let's brush it off and get back up.

01:04:01.254 --> 01:04:03.340
Grandma.

01:04:04.799 --> 01:04:06.968
[sobs]

01:04:09.387 --> 01:04:11.931
-[music fades]
-[rain pattering]

01:04:13.475 --> 01:04:15.602
[loud clatter]

01:04:18.772 --> 01:04:19.981
Grandma.

01:04:31.576 --> 01:04:32.702
Grandma?

01:04:41.920 --> 01:04:43.254
Grandma.

01:04:46.132 --> 01:04:47.300
Grandma?

01:04:48.093 --> 01:04:49.135
[sighs]

01:04:50.804 --> 01:04:53.556
Why aren't you answering me?

01:04:54.224 --> 01:04:55.308
Grand…

01:04:59.854 --> 01:05:02.065
[somber music playing]

01:05:03.149 --> 01:05:04.192
Grandma!

01:05:05.235 --> 01:05:06.653
Grandma!

01:05:06.736 --> 01:05:08.905
Grandma, are you okay?

01:05:08.988 --> 01:05:11.116
Please wake up! Grandma!

01:05:11.199 --> 01:05:13.243
[gasps] Where's the phone?

01:05:13.326 --> 01:05:15.078
The phone.

01:05:15.161 --> 01:05:16.663
[sobbing]

01:05:20.583 --> 01:05:21.793
[whimpers]

01:05:24.587 --> 01:05:26.631
Oh no, Grandma!

01:05:35.723 --> 01:05:39.602
[trembling] Hang in there, Grandma.
Please, please…

01:05:39.686 --> 01:05:41.729
-[sobbing]
-[somber music continues]

01:05:46.651 --> 01:05:49.028
-Grandma…
-[music turns daring]

01:05:49.112 --> 01:05:50.613
Come on!

01:05:56.619 --> 01:06:00.582
[whimpers, grunts]

01:06:01.666 --> 01:06:03.209
[wailing]

01:06:03.293 --> 01:06:06.838
[trembling] Someone, please help.

01:06:08.131 --> 01:06:09.757
Please help!

01:06:12.260 --> 01:06:14.012
-Help me.
-[banging on door]

01:06:14.095 --> 01:06:15.722
Save my grandma!

01:06:15.805 --> 01:06:18.099
Please save my grandma.

01:06:18.183 --> 01:06:20.435
[sobbing]

01:06:21.436 --> 01:06:22.979
Hello?

01:06:23.062 --> 01:06:24.522
Anyone home?

01:06:24.606 --> 01:06:27.108
[sobbing]

01:06:27.192 --> 01:06:28.818
[screaming] Anyone?

01:06:29.486 --> 01:06:31.571
Please, save her!

01:06:31.654 --> 01:06:34.032
-[Mi-ji sobbing]
-[daring music continues]

01:06:44.584 --> 01:06:47.212
[music fades]

01:06:47.295 --> 01:06:49.422
[Ho-su] I talked to your team leader.

01:06:50.131 --> 01:06:52.509
We'll reschedule
after Ms. Ro-sa is discharged.

01:06:59.849 --> 01:07:01.851
What was that earlier?

01:07:02.352 --> 01:07:04.354
You were having trouble breathing.

01:07:04.437 --> 01:07:06.105
Is that your heart again? Or…

01:07:06.189 --> 01:07:07.357
[Mi-ji] Thank you.

01:07:09.651 --> 01:07:10.610
For what?

01:07:12.946 --> 01:07:14.572
For everything.

01:07:14.656 --> 01:07:16.658
The meeting, and Ms. Ro-sa.

01:07:17.283 --> 01:07:19.994
If it weren't for you,
everything would've gone wrong.

01:07:20.078 --> 01:07:22.372
I only went because you told me about her.

01:07:27.877 --> 01:07:29.712
Don't worry too much about Ms. Ro-sa.

01:07:29.796 --> 01:07:31.881
The doctor said we made it just in time.

01:07:31.965 --> 01:07:33.716
We got here before it was too late.

01:07:38.471 --> 01:07:40.682
Would it have been
the same for my grandma?

01:07:43.518 --> 01:07:45.562
The day she collapsed…

01:07:45.645 --> 01:07:48.064
If someone other than Mi-ji
had been with her,

01:07:49.732 --> 01:07:51.568
would things have turned out better?

01:07:52.110 --> 01:07:53.319
[pensive music playing]

01:07:53.403 --> 01:07:54.612
I think so.

01:07:55.905 --> 01:07:57.699
Even the hospital said so.

01:07:57.782 --> 01:07:59.701
That we should've gotten there sooner.

01:08:00.827 --> 01:08:02.912
If it hadn't been for Mi-ji,

01:08:02.996 --> 01:08:05.748
Grandma might not be bedridden
like she is now.

01:08:08.293 --> 01:08:09.419
How is that…

01:08:10.628 --> 01:08:11.546
Mi-ji's fault?

01:08:11.629 --> 01:08:13.131
Then whose fault is it?

01:08:13.881 --> 01:08:15.633
She's always like that.

01:08:15.717 --> 01:08:19.262
It's not enough that she's miserable.
She drags everyone else down with her.

01:08:19.345 --> 01:08:20.305
Mi-rae.

01:08:20.888 --> 01:08:22.849
You know what I hate the most?

01:08:22.932 --> 01:08:24.934
That she keeps on living like that.

01:08:25.018 --> 01:08:27.478
While Grandma's lying there
because of her,

01:08:27.562 --> 01:08:31.441
she still laughs, eats, and goes out
like she didn't do anything.

01:08:50.960 --> 01:08:52.003
[sighs]

01:08:53.504 --> 01:08:55.632
Then I guess
my dad died because of me.

01:08:57.383 --> 01:08:58.301
What?

01:09:00.261 --> 01:09:02.138
[music fades]

01:09:02.221 --> 01:09:03.765
The day he died…

01:09:06.225 --> 01:09:07.685
I insisted we go out.

01:09:08.561 --> 01:09:09.854
[soft melancholic music playing]

01:09:09.937 --> 01:09:11.814
I didn't want to go on any other day,

01:09:12.732 --> 01:09:14.484
and I didn't want to go with Mom.

01:09:17.070 --> 01:09:18.571
I wanted it to be just us two.

01:09:19.989 --> 01:09:21.574
I got my way in the end.

01:09:23.910 --> 01:09:25.495
And the car ended up totaled.

01:09:26.454 --> 01:09:28.039
A drunk driver crashed into us.

01:09:35.588 --> 01:09:38.174
Dad died, and I survived.

01:09:40.677 --> 01:09:44.097
If I hadn't insisted that day,
he might still be alive.

01:09:44.180 --> 01:09:45.306
That's…

01:09:46.265 --> 01:09:49.686
That's not your fault.
It's the drunk driver's fault.

01:09:49.769 --> 01:09:52.271
Then why would you say
stuff like that about Mi-ji?

01:09:53.981 --> 01:09:56.526
You tell me it's not my fault,

01:09:56.609 --> 01:09:58.236
yet you're so harsh with her.

01:10:01.406 --> 01:10:04.075
Just like no one was to blame
for what happened today,

01:10:05.034 --> 01:10:07.704
what happened to your grandma
isn’t on Mi-ji either.

01:10:09.831 --> 01:10:12.709
-I guess.
-You guess? It's the truth.

01:10:13.876 --> 01:10:15.545
How is any of that Mi-ji's fault?

01:10:18.047 --> 01:10:20.049
Okay, I get it--

01:10:20.133 --> 01:10:21.592
[Ho-su] No. Be clear about it.

01:10:24.303 --> 01:10:25.847
It wasn't Mi-ji's fault.

01:10:25.930 --> 01:10:27.974
[soft melancholic music continues]

01:10:43.865 --> 01:10:47.744
[music concludes]

01:10:53.541 --> 01:10:55.001
Mm!

01:10:55.084 --> 01:10:58.463
You know, jam tastes best
when the strawberries are a bit tart.

01:10:59.088 --> 01:11:01.382
If they're too sweet, they're not as good.

01:11:04.218 --> 01:11:06.554
You've been working hard
on the farm, right?

01:11:07.221 --> 01:11:08.890
I wouldn't say hard…

01:11:08.973 --> 01:11:10.183
I see.

01:11:11.934 --> 01:11:16.355
Things don't always feel right
in the beginning.

01:11:16.939 --> 01:11:19.442
If you start with something super sweet

01:11:19.525 --> 01:11:22.737
and try something sweet and tangy,
all you can taste is the tang.

01:11:22.820 --> 01:11:25.990
But life's funny, you know?

01:11:27.116 --> 01:11:28.159
Just like strawberries.

01:11:28.242 --> 01:11:33.414
Even if it feels too sour right now,
the tart ones make the best jam.

01:11:35.208 --> 01:11:38.669
Did you get it?

01:11:38.753 --> 01:11:41.088
I'm using strawberries
as a metaphor for life.

01:11:41.672 --> 01:11:44.008
[chuckles softly] Yes.

01:11:44.091 --> 01:11:46.469
Oh, you did? [laughs]

01:11:46.552 --> 01:11:48.179
Can you stir this for a bit?

01:12:01.484 --> 01:12:03.736
You're looking at that photo again?

01:12:03.820 --> 01:12:04.821
[Mi-rae] Sorry?

01:12:07.657 --> 01:12:10.409
Be honest. This is Mi-rae, right?

01:12:11.494 --> 01:12:12.870
No, it's not.

01:12:12.954 --> 01:12:14.455
Come on.

01:12:14.539 --> 01:12:17.792
Even I can recognize Mi-rae at that age.

01:12:18.626 --> 01:12:20.253
She always had that look.

01:12:22.088 --> 01:12:23.089
What look?

01:12:23.172 --> 01:12:25.132
Like she was holding it all in.

01:12:25.216 --> 01:12:26.926
Trying to hide her soft side.

01:12:27.009 --> 01:12:28.970
[gentle music playing]

01:12:29.053 --> 01:12:33.224
She may look sullen on the outside,

01:12:33.307 --> 01:12:36.143
but kids as thoughtful
and kind as her are rare.

01:12:38.271 --> 01:12:39.897
She's not that kind.

01:12:39.981 --> 01:12:41.274
What do you mean?

01:12:42.483 --> 01:12:43.860
Of course she is.

01:12:43.943 --> 01:12:48.072
She was nice enough to cut her hair short
just so her sister could graduate.

01:12:48.656 --> 01:12:50.491
Mi-ji, don't be like that.

01:12:50.992 --> 01:12:53.160
No one cares more about family
than Mi-rae.

01:12:55.955 --> 01:12:57.707
[Mi-rae] For so long,

01:12:58.249 --> 01:13:01.919
I was harder on myself than anyone else,
just for being me.

01:13:03.504 --> 01:13:07.800
Even deer and hermit crabs
do everything they can to survive.

01:13:08.718 --> 01:13:10.011
So why do humans…

01:13:10.094 --> 01:13:11.804
SENDER: YU MI-JI

01:13:11.888 --> 01:13:13.639
RECIPIENT: YU MI-RAE

01:13:14.140 --> 01:13:17.643
Why do I end up attacking myself

01:13:18.311 --> 01:13:20.521
in the moments
I most need to protect myself?

01:13:21.314 --> 01:13:23.649
[gentle music continues]

01:13:37.163 --> 01:13:39.332
[Mi-ji] It wasn't until
I lived as someone else

01:13:39.415 --> 01:13:42.960
that I realized my worst enemy was myself.

01:13:45.671 --> 01:13:49.175
Now I know, but so what?
What difference does it make?

01:13:51.719 --> 01:13:53.679
[music fades]

01:13:54.305 --> 01:13:56.140
Why are you defending Mi-ji?

01:13:56.223 --> 01:13:58.142
You're not even that close.

01:14:00.978 --> 01:14:02.063
Because I like her.

01:14:07.151 --> 01:14:08.486
What?

01:14:10.863 --> 01:14:12.031
You already know.

01:14:13.157 --> 01:14:14.700
Mi-ji is my first love.

01:14:15.409 --> 01:14:17.995
[dreamy tender music playing]

01:14:23.793 --> 01:14:25.544
[Mi-ji] Knowing doesn't mean

01:14:26.379 --> 01:14:27.838
I can change anything.

01:14:27.922 --> 01:14:30.841
-[singing in Korean]
-[romantic pop song playing]

01:14:30.925 --> 01:14:37.348
[singing in Korean continues]

01:14:39.767 --> 01:14:45.606
[singing in Korean continues]

01:14:45.690 --> 01:14:51.404
[singing in Korean continues]

01:14:52.571 --> 01:14:54.532
[singing in Korean continues]

01:14:54.615 --> 01:14:55.783
YU MI-JI

01:14:55.866 --> 01:14:57.952
[man] Is this team in charge
of the new HQ project?

01:14:58.035 --> 01:14:59.996
Ms. Yu, prepare the project report
by next week.

01:15:00.079 --> 01:15:01.914
-What?
-[Gyeong-min] If you can't, then say so.

01:15:01.998 --> 01:15:04.542
-The penalty will be all yours too.
-Can you help me?

01:15:04.625 --> 01:15:07.420
-[Se-jin] Did you receive this?
-Mi-ji, that's not fair.

01:15:07.503 --> 01:15:09.171
I hear you're dating the farm owner.

01:15:09.255 --> 01:15:11.090
Is that just a false rumor?

01:15:11.173 --> 01:15:14.135
-[Mi-rae] Does my response even matter?
-Hey, Ho-su!

01:15:14.218 --> 01:15:15.761
Let's keep this strictly professional.

01:15:15.845 --> 01:15:17.972
I'm Ms. Kim Ro-sa's
legal representative, Lee Ho-su.

01:15:18.055 --> 01:15:20.474
Are you going
to keep treating me like this?

01:15:20.558 --> 01:15:22.351
Why are you curious about that?

01:15:22.435 --> 01:15:26.230
[singing in Korean continues]

01:15:26.313 --> 01:15:30.026
[singing in Korean continues]

01:15:32.280 --> 01:15:34.280
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
